    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55299": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | NC New Teacher Instructional Support Coach Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources NC New Teacher Instructional Support Coach Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List of References with Contact Information Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title NC New Teacher Instructional Support Coach Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank Position Number 092061 Department College of Education - 260000 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The NC New Teacher Support Program is seeking an Instructional Coach to support beginning teachers through consistent, individualized, in-the-moment coaching aligned to individualized growth and personalized professional development. The primary role of the NC New Teacher Support Program Instructional Coach 10 month position is to support beginning teachers through the delivery of the program’s three core services: 10 professional learning institute, 2) individualized instructional coaching, and 3) aligned professional development. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree and current NC teaching license required Minimum of five years teaching experience with measurable student outcomes License/Certification Required current NC teaching license Preferred Qualifications Experience leading adult professional learning Knowledge of NC Standard Course of Study, NC Professional Teaching Standards, NC DPI Induction Program, Mentor Standards and teacher leadership standards Skilled in data collection, analysis, and evidence-based decision-making Strong collaboration, communication, and technology skills Approachable, collaborative, reflective, motivating, and solutions-focused Highly knowledgeable of the Teaching Fellows program and initiatives Essential Duties and Responsibilities Instructional Coaching & Teacher Support Facilitate collaborative, non-evaluative and iterative coaching cycles, both in-person and virtual, based on individual teacher needs utilizing the following research-based components: • Individualized goal setting Lesson planning Share and model high-impact instructional strategies Co-teaching Observation & reflective feedback Analysis of student work/evidence Analysis of formative & summative assessment data Teacher leadership development Support and use instructional technology Utilize program-approved instructional coaching resources and platforms Professional Learning & Collaboration Design and facilitate professional learning sessions/institute (in-person & virtual) Build teacher learning networks within the hub & state Align professional learning with district and school priorities Connect teachers to district, university, state, and national resources Program Leadership & Development Collaborate with NC NTSP coaches and program office, school district faculty/staff, IHE faculty/staff, and state level agencies to improve program delivery Actively engage in ongoing professional learning to further develop coaching expertise and program initiatives Collect and report data on coaching services, teacher growth, student outcomes, and research initiatives Actively serve on NC NTSP committees and design teams Support and implement the research and development initiatives of the NC NTSP and research partners Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Mon-Fri, hours may vary according for travel time to school districts Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 10 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $57,000-$60,000 (10 Month Salary) Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/17/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 07/31/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 08/17/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List of References with Contact Information Search Chair Name Monica Lambert Search Chair Email lambertma@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55273 Posting Number 201501817P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a North Carolina Teaching License? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information License/Certification Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
