    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55760": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 095401 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Psychology - 250800 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications PhD or PsyD from an APA -accredited doctoral program with a specialization in Clinical Psychology, including combined clinical programs (e.g., Clinical/School Psychology). ABD candidates will be considered, but the degree should be expected by the time the position begins. More advanced candidates currently in a tenure-track position can request time awarded towards the tenure clock. By the start of appointment, must be licensed or license-eligible as a Psychologist, Health Service Provider in North Carolina through the NC Psychology Board. Evidence of success or potential for developing significant research, quality publications, and external funding. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) Clinical and/or research experience relevant to children and adolescents, or rural communities. Interest in teaching cognitive assessment. Completion of an APA / CPA -accredited internship. Clinical supervision experience. Teaching experience at undergraduate or graduate level. License/Certification Required See Minimum Qualifications Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Psychology has 43 full-time faculty members (33 tenure-track) and serves more than 1,400 undergraduate majors and 90 graduate students across four graduate programs: Psychological Science MA, Industrial-Organizational Psychology and Human Resource Management MA, School Psychology MA/ SSP , and Clinical Psychology PsyD. Faculty are afforded the opportunity to teach summer courses for supplementary income and engage in external activities for up to one day per week, which many clinical faculty use for consultation or private practice endeavors. The Department aims to guide and support new junior faculty, specifically by limiting service requirements, minimizing new course preparations and teaching workload in the first year, and ongoing mentoring throughout the tenure process. The department is dedicated to the mission and strategic plan of the university and to creating a nurturing community that welcomes, respects, and supports all constituents. Additional information about the Department of Psychology, the University, and the surrounding area is located on the Psychology website . The Department proudly offers a Clinical Psychology Psy.D. program that embraces a scholar-practitioner philosophy and a small cohort, mentor match model. We provide assistantship funding to all students for four years. This program is specifically designed to develop empirically-informed clinical psychologists who are prepared to serve as generalists in rural areas. We offer a rigorous program of study and are committed to providing high-quality, evidence-based training. The program is currently accredited by APA on contingency, with the application for full accreditation to be submitted in 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The typical teaching load is three courses per semester. Maintain a productive program of research, including publishing in peer-reviewed journals. Supervise undergraduate and graduate students’ research including foundational projects and dissertations. Seek external funding (e.g., research, workforce development, outreach, student funding). Provide professional service to the program, department, university, community, and discipline. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy and Interests 4. Statement of Research Interests 5. Unofficial graduate transcripts 6. List of references with contact information (minimum of 3) UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 07/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/01/2026 Search Chair Name Denise Martz Search Chair Email martzdm@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54269 Posting Number FA00583P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Interests Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54570": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Catering &amp; Special Event Bartender Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Catering & Special Event Bartender Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be reviewed by the Catering department based on employment needs. Please include the following document(s): Resume List of 3 professional references Cover Letter (optional) Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Catering & Special Event Bartender Location Boone, NC Position Number B32305 Department Catering - 170400 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Minimum age 21 years old Experience in bartending or service activities in a restaurant, country club, event venue, commercial kitchen or other hospitality space. Equivalent training will also be considered License/Certification Required Alcohol Seller-Server Training Program by eTIPS, ABC , ALE or other approved resource. (May be completed once hired.) Essential Job Functions Grandview Catering & Events provides handcrafted fare and unique experiences brought to life by culinary and event professionals. We focus on attention to detail, quality ingredients and sustainable practices with exceptional customer service. We proudly serve Appalachian State University campuses as well as off-site events for university affiliated businesses, community members and alumni with Grandview Ballroom featured as our premiere event space. What You’ll Do: As a Grandview Bartender, you’ll help bring a wide variety of events to life from vibrant student celebrations and campus traditions to high-profile donor galas and local community gatherings. Events may be on weekday afternoons/evenings, or weekends, and scheudling options are flexible. Your main responsibilities will include: Crafting the Experience: Greet guests with a smile, mix classic cocktails, pour beer and wine confidently, and keep the good vibes flowing throughout the event. Bar Setup & Styling: Help the Hospitality team by setting up bars with linens, glassware, ice, and products. Event Execution: Work events from start to finish alongside a team. This includes arriving on time, providing stellar service, and wrapping up with a smooth event breakdown. Keeping it Sharp: Maintain a clean, organized, and efficient bar area while looking professional. While the majority of our events feature standard beer and wine service, you will also have the opportunity to utilize basic mixology skills and practice safe alcohol service at select premium events. Handling Sales: Use user-friendly, handheld point-of-sale devices to process guest payments accurately. Being a Team Player: Stay in sync with your supervisors and coworkers, build relationships with our diverse team (including awesome student staff), and jump in to help with other team duties as assigned. This highly flexible role features a varying schedule based on our booked events, making it the perfect opportunity for someone looking to easily pick up just a few shifts a month. Preferred Qualifications Full-service bar experience, especially with liquor mixed drinks Available to work occasional weekends and evenings. Work Schedule/Hours Hours, days, and frequency will change depending on business needs. Catering employees are required to work special events including, but not limited to, home football games, University commencement, other large scale events Number of Hours Per Week Varies Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $20.00 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 06/05/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be reviewed by the Catering department based on employment needs. Please include the following document(s): Resume List of 3 professional references Cover Letter (optional) Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54563 Posting Number 201500854P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you at least 21 years of age? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53158": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Art History and Art Management Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Art History and Art Management Adjunct Instructor Pool Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Art History and Art Management Adjunct Instructor Pool Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter – the letter should include a list of which Art History or Art Management courses you would be qualiﬁed to teach and your approach to those courses. Curriculum vitae List of references with contact information Sample teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, previous teaching evaluations) are encouraged but not required upon initial application (attach under optional Evidence of Teaching), Ofﬁcial transcripts will be required at a later stage of hire consideration. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Art History and Art Management Adjunct Instructor Pool Department Art - 265050 Location Boone, NC Position Number 018863 Description of Department The Department of Art is accredited by NASAD and has 47 full-time faculty members, over 20 part-time faculty members, over 800 undergraduate majors and offers the following degrees: BFAs in Art Education, Graphic Design, Photography with concentrations in Commercial and Fine Art, and Studio Art; a BA in Art & Visual Culture with concentrations in Art History, Art Management and Studio Art; and a BS in Graphic Communications Management with concentrations in Cross Media Production and Print/Packaging Production. The Department of Art typically offers a range of travel opportunities including trips to the university’s New York Loft and has offered study abroad trips to China, Costa Rica, Cuba, Italy, Japan, the Netherlands, Scotland, Spain, and Taiwan. Additional information about the department, the university, and the surrounding area can be found at art.appstate.edu. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications MA or MFA , art history/ visual studies, curatorial studies, art administration, or related discipline. Essential Job Functions The Department of Art seeks to hire multiple adjunct instructors for various courses in art history, visual culture, and art management for the academic year 2026-27 Instruction may be face-to-face or online, depending on need. Essential job functions include course preparation and delivery, grading, student engagement, and weekly ofﬁce hours. Instructors are expected to submit materials for departmental and/or General Education assessment as requested by the department chair. Courses taught may include: ARH 2030: Global Art History: Prehistory -1400 ARH 2130: Global Art History: 1400 – Present Other courses depending on department need and instructor expertise are welcome. Applicants may also propose a topic not currently included among those listed in the course catalog (please see the list of courses for Art History and Art Management .) Preferred Qualifications ABD or PhD in art history/ visual studies or related discipline. Relevant teaching experience Experience teaching online asynchronous courses Experience with and enthusiasm for teaching undergraduate General Education courses Number of Hours Per Week Varies based on course schedule (maximum 5 courses per academic year) Number of Months per Year 9 Hiring Range Commensurate with qualifications and equity.   Master's Degree - $3588 per 3 credit hour course; Doctorate/Terminal Degree - $3987 per 3 credit hour course Posting Details Posting Date 10/24/2023 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire 01/16/2024 Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/24/2023 Search Chair Name Heather Waldroup Search Chair Email waldrouphl@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter – the letter should include a list of which Art History or Art Management courses you would be qualiﬁed to teach and your approach to those courses. Curriculum vitae List of references with contact information Sample teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, previous teaching evaluations) are encouraged but not required upon initial application (attach under optional Evidence of Teaching), Ofﬁcial transcripts will be required at a later stage of hire consideration. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which of the following best describes your interest and experience teaching fully online courses? I am not interested in teaching online courses I am interested in teaching online courses, but I have no previous experience. I have previous experience teaching online courses and would be interested in teaching online for App State Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
