    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55374": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Catering Coordination Assistant",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Catering Coordination Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Catering Coordination Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Catering Coordination Assistant Location Boone, NC Position Number A32305 Department Catering - 170400 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Must pass a Criminal Background Check Ability to work with people from diverse cultures and backgrounds Ability to professionally represent the program/department Ability to work independently 1 year of relevant experience in Food and Beverage, Hospitality, Dining, Customer Service, Administrative, or other related area. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Grandview Catering & Events provides handcrafted fare and unique experiences brought to life by culinary and event professionals inspired by the latest trends and classic comforts. We focus on attention to detail, quality ingredients and sustainable practices with exceptional customer service. We proudly serve Appalachian State University campuses as well as off-site events for university affiliated businesses, community members and alumni with Grandview Ballroom featured as our premiere event space. We’re looking for a driven individual to hit the ground running and join our growing team. The successful candidate will work with others to ensure our daily catering operations and special events run efficiently while upholding our excellent customer service. What You’ll Do: We’re looking for a driven, detail-oriented individual to join our growing team. As a Coordination Assistant, you’ll work behind the scenes to recieve requests, book events and help ensure our daily catering operations and special events run seamlessly, all while delivering top-tier customer service to the Appalachian State community and beyond. Your Main Responsibilities Include: Pipeline & Host Outreach: Track incoming leads and service requests. Proactively reach out to event hosts to clarify catering options as needed, follow up on room reservations that are missing catering requests, and review requests for external vendors. Catering Order Management: Take ownership of pickup orders and assigned catering events -handling everything from initial proposals and client communication to menu creation, internal documentation, and post-event follow-up. Client & Event Support: Attend client meetings and site visits alongside managers to take notes, gather details, and assist in bringing the client’s vision to life. Administrative Operations: Partner directly with the Event Coordinator and Director on administrative tasks, including reviewing host feedback and refining internal processes. Team Communication: Maintain open, frequent communication with supervisors and team members regarding event status, logistics, questions, and fresh ideas. Participate in team meetings. Culture & Collaboration: Build positive, professional working relationships with coworkers and student staff, while jumping in to support the wider Grandview team on other duties as assigned. Preferred Qualifications Excellent communication skills for conversing with clients, guests and employees Time management and organizational skills Experience in customer service and/or food and beverage service Work Schedule/Hours 15-20 hours/week, typically between Monday-Friday 9:00-5:00 Schedule may vary depending on business needs Catering employees are required to work special events including, but not limited to, home football games, University commencement, other large scale events Number of Hours Per Week 15-20 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position N/A Hiring Range $16.00-$21.00 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55338 Posting Number 201501105P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55990": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Parent to Parent Outreach and Family Services Coordinator, Watauga County",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Parent to Parent Outreach and Family Services Coordinator, Watauga County Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Parent to Parent Outreach and Family Services Coordinator, Watauga County Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Parent to Parent Outreach and Family Services Coordinator, Watauga County Location Boone, NC Position Number N07362 Department Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness - 273600 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in a health and human services field or five (5) years case management and/or lived experience. Degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required Not applicable Essential Job Functions Job Description: The Outreach and Family Services Coordinator provides family navigation, case management, and outreach services to families of children with special needs. This position plays a key role in community engagement by facilitating parent-to-parent matches, facilitating support groups, and delivering educational workshops. Additionally, the role includes working within the Growing Well Clinic to assist with quality improvement initiatives and family support services. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: Family Navigation & Case Management: Provide individualized support to families, connecting them to appropriate healthcare, educational, and community resources. Parent-to-Parent Support: Facilitate parent matches, coordinate Circle of Parents Support Groups, and provide guidance to caregivers navigating the challenges of raising a child with special needs. Educational Workshops & Outreach: Organize and assist in delivering Triple P seminars and training sessions for parents and caregivers, and other educational workshops as requested. Quality Improvement Initiatives: Participate in continuous improvement efforts for the Growing Well Clinic, contributing to enhanced service delivery and patient outcomes. Community Collaboration: Work with DSS , CDSA , public schools, and healthcare providers to strengthen partnerships and streamline services for families. Program Monitoring & Reporting: Maintain accurate records of family interactions, referrals, and program activities for reporting and compliance purposes. Preferred Qualifications Experience Preferences: Lived experience caring for child(ren) or youth with special health care needs. Work Schedule/Hours Monday-Friday Occasional weekends. Number of Hours Per Week 25 hours per week Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position Must be able to lift 25 lbs for equipment purposes. Hiring Range $23.00 per hour Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date 09/18/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55939 Posting Number 201501139P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation (1st doc) Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
