    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55506": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Director of Digital Learning and Educational Innovation",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Director of Digital Learning and Educational Innovation Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Director of Digital Learning and Educational Innovation Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submission Materials: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Cover letter specifically addressing the required and preferred qualifications for the position. Miscellaneous: A Statement discussing the following: 1) their views on technology and its potential for educational innovation 2) their vision of their role in this position and the Reich College of Education Technology and Educational Innovation Media lab. This statement should be a maximum of one-page, single-spaced, 12 point font. Contact information for three professional references. Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Director of Digital Learning and Educational Innovation Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank Position Number 062751 Department College of Education - 260000 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Reich College of Education ( RCOE ) is the designated professional education unit at Appalachian State University. The College offers a broad range of comprehensive degree programs at the baccalaureate, master’s, specialist, and doctoral levels, as well as programs leading to certificates and licensure. The College is committed to providing a well-balanced program of classroom and clinical experiences and emphasizes: programs of rigor and excellence; bold initiatives that address emerging societal needs through innovative programs, teaching strategies, and technologies; the integration of broad perspectives and global awareness across all program areas; the development and delivery of a comprehensive body of knowledge within each discipline; and active engagement and collaboration with communities and stakeholders. The purpose of this position is to support and advance the mission of the RCOE through strategic leadership in digital teaching, learning, and educational innovation. The Director systematically assesses and responds to program, departmental, and college needs related to instructional technology and digital learning competencies; supports faculty, staff, and students in the effective integration of digital tools, media, and innovative pedagogies; and fosters the development of high-quality, technology-enhanced instruction, research, and outreach. The position oversees the RCOE Media Lab as a hub for digital scholarship, instructional innovation, and media production; provides guidance on emerging technologies and digital infrastructure; and supports planning, resource allocation, and equipment management. The Director collaborates with campus partners to advance institutional digital learning initiatives, contributes to and supports externally funded research and grant development, mentors students and project staff, and promotes interdisciplinary partnerships that strengthen the college’s leadership in digital and technology-enhanced education. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in a relevant field (i.e. instructional technology, instructional design, educational media, instructional systems design, technology or related field) from an accredited university and 10+ years of experience License/Certification Required N/A Preferred Qualifications Earned Doctorate in a relevant field (i.e. instructional technology, instructional design, educational media, instructional systems design, technology or related field) from an accredited university and relative experience. Evidence of successful teaching or instructional experience in higher education, public schools or professional learning environments. Experience facilitating faculty development for the purpose of integrating technology in a variety of settings. Experience with emerging technologies Skill in applying computer hardware and software and related technologies for educational innovation; experience with mixed platforms. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. Experience managing student and related workers. Ability to conduct and collaborate on research related to digital teaching and learning, technology integration, and innovation in education. Ability to oversee digital learning resources, purchasing, technology planning and equipment inventory associated with Media/Educational innovation lab. Experience managing or supporting a media lab, makerspace, or similar innovation-focused environment Record of externally funded research tied to educational innovation or technology. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide Strategic Leadership in Digital Learning and Educational Innovation Lead and support college-wide initiatives that advance digital teaching, learning, and educational innovation Work with RCOE Strategic Planning group on initiatives involving digital technologies Collaborate with academic departments to integrate digital pedagogies, media, and instructional technologies into programs and courses Serve as a liaison with campus partners Chair the RCOE Technology Advisory Committee Support Instructional Innovation and Faculty, Staff and Student Engagement Provide consultation, professional learning opportunities, and individualized support to faculty on effective use of digital tools and innovative pedagogies Support the design, development, and continuous improvement of technology-enhanced and online learning experiences Promote effective and scalable practices for digital instruction across modalities Assist with the On-boarding of Adjunct Faculty in the areas of digital learning and educational innovation Work with Digital Learning Competencies for Faculty/Teacher Candidates Work with Professional Education Core Curriculum Director for cross-walking/inclusion of DLCs in core courses Support Staff Members in Digital Business Processes Advance Research, Grants, and Scholarly Innovation Contribute to and support externally funded research and grant development related to digital learning, educational technology, and media innovation Foster interdisciplinary collaboration that strengthens the college’s research and innovation capacity Engage in scholarship related to digital teaching and learning Oversee Media Lab Operations and Digital Infrastructure Provide leadership and oversight for the RCOE Media Lab, including operations, staffing, equipment, and services Guide planning, purchasing, and management of digital learning technologies and resources Evaluate and recommend enhancements to media, technology, and digital learning infrastructure Mentor and Support Students and Project Staff Supervise and mentor graduate assistants, student workers, and project staff involved in digital learning and media initiatives Support student engagement in digital scholarship, media production, and innovative learning experiences Support College and University Collaboration and Service Partner with college and university leadership on initiatives related to digital transformation in education Contribute to planning, implementation, and assessment of college-level digital learning priorities Serve on committees and support strategic initiatives aligned with the mission of the RCOE Provide support for Accreditation and Program Approval Efforts Related to Digital Technologies Perform Other Duties as Assigned Carry out additional responsibilities as identified by the Dean of the Reich College of Education Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Mon-Fri, 8:00 - 5:00 p.m. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $90,000 - $100,919 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 08/19/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 09/21/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Submission Materials: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Cover letter specifically addressing the required and preferred qualifications for the position. Miscellaneous: A Statement discussing the following: 1) their views on technology and its potential for educational innovation 2) their vision of their role in this position and the Reich College of Education Technology and Educational Innovation Media lab. This statement should be a maximum of one-page, single-spaced, 12 point font. Contact information for three professional references. Search Chair Name Amy Milsom Search Chair Email milsomas@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55322 Posting Number 201501819P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Miscellaneous (Explanation in Applicant Instructions) List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54718": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Public Administration",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Public Administration Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Public Administration Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Public Administration Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 067821 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Government & Justice Studies - 250750 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in Public Administration, Political Science, or a related discipline is required at the time of appointment, but ABDs will be considered. A J.D. is not sufficient for this position. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) Areas of interest are open, however, there is a particular interest for candidates with expertise in public policy analysis and program evaluation. Professional experience in Public Administration, particularly at the local or state level and/or in non-profit management, is desirable. License/Certification Required Description of the Department or Unit The Master of Public Administration program is NASPAA -accredited and has approximately 60 students, most of whom specialize in local government or non-profit administration (see mpa.appstate.edu). The Department houses undergraduate programs in criminal justice and political science and graduate programs in public administration and political science. Additional information about the Department of Government and Justice Studies can be found at http://gjs.appstate.edu. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The teaching load is three courses per semester for faculty who maintain an active research agenda. Responsibilities include instruction at the graduate and undergraduate levels, an active program of scholarship, instruction on-campus (Boone and Hickory), as well as online instruction, student advising, and participation in service activities. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: A letter of application/interest Current vita; Contact information for three references familiar with the candidate who can speak to the candidate’s teaching and scholarship qualifications. an unofficial copy of graduate (and doctorate, if applicable) transcripts For additional information and inquiries, contact Yong Hur (hury@appstate.edu). Review of complete applications will begin 9/8/26, and will continue until the position is filled. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 06/15/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/08/2026 Search Chair Name Yong Hur Search Chair Email hury@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54232 Posting Number FA00586P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55997": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Housekeeper (2nd Shift)  Multiple Vacancies Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Housekeeper (2nd Shift)  Multiple Vacancies Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please list a minimum of 3 professional references in the application. Appalachian State University Benefits Information: https://hr.appstate.edu/hr-services/benefits Finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check. Applicant must have a valid driver’s license to be considered. Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Building Environmental Services Technician (Building Services) Working Title Housekeeper (2nd Shift)  Multiple Vacancies Location Boone, NC Job Category 8 Position Number 032881 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Facilities Operations - Environmental Services - 410600 Primary Purpose of Position Provide cleaning services for areas within Academic, Sporting and Event affiliated facilities of the University which consists of more than three million square feet. Provide setup and breakdown of all types of equipment and apparatuses used by sports programs and special events. Demonstrates a variety of skills, in multiple trades, to maintain facilities for accommodation of various uses including academics, sporting events, special events and use by the public. Maintain a campus environment which is functional, attractive, safe, and conducive to a cost-effective manner. Personnel are required to train to their potential in order to achieve the most effective development methodology to obtain the greatest output from all resources. Minimum Qualifications Some knowledge of cleaning procedures, ability to follow instructions and to perform medium to heavy physical work; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Special certification may be required for some of these positions.- License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions If employee is assigned to work in a designated security sensitive area, employee is required to undergo an extensive background check under the administration of the ASU Police Department and complete a Security Awareness Training as required. Floor Maintenance which consists, at a minimum, of daily sweeping, wet mopping, periodic spray-buffing and high speed burnishing, scheduled stripping and refinishing of resilient floors. Restroom Sanitation which consists of, at a minimum, daily sweeping, mopping, cleaning mirrors, spot cleaning walls and stall partitions, applying disinfectant cleaners. Check and refill towel, soap, deodorant and tissue containers. Periodic scrubbing of all surfaces with hard brushes and floor scrubber. Scrubbing of fixture surfaces with hand pad and bowl cleaners. Dusting, polishing and Spot cleaning which consists of, at a minimum, daily cleaning of all furniture including desks, chairs, bookshelves, filing cabinets, window sills and ledges, stair railings, etc. Cleaning of walls, boards, light fixtures, air handling units, blinds, ceilings and interior/exterior glass. Vacuuming and Spot cleaning of carpeted floors which includes determining chemical and/or cleaner to be used for particular spots / spills. Trash and debris which consists of, at a minimum, removal of trash, recycling and other foreign matter from trash containers and building surfaces. Replacement of trash can liners as needed. Removal of trash, snow and other debris from entrances, steps and sidewalks. Chemicals, Supplies, and Equipment involves the proper use of various types of chemicals including detergents, disinfectants, finishes, etc., associated with housekeeping duties. Must understand and follow manufacturer’s label instructions on application, dilution rates, protective gear, safety precautions and proper storage of all chemicals used. Must understand and institute set routines and procedures established for chemical use. Keep housekeeping closets clean with supplies stored neatly and in an accessible order. Supply inventory must be maintained at a proper level for availability. Must understand and institute set guidelines of equipment to insure the right type of equipment or machine is used for required work. Security consists of responsibility for keys that give access to assigned areas. Unlocking and locking of building doors at designated (scheduled) times is required. Valid driver’s license and knowledge, skills and abilities to operate university vehicles, as needed. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Must be able to follow oral and written instructions. Must be physically able to lift moderately heavy materials, equipment and supplies on a daily basis. Ability to work steadily, periodically in extreme temperatures for duration of shift. Must be able to complete work repair requests and requisition forms. Must have full use of all five senses. Good communication skills and abilities when dealing with faculty, staff and students, thus fostering good relations with the public and building occupants. Ability to work with cleaning chemicals. Ability to work all academic building, sporting facilities and other campus event venues, as assigned, including reassignment of supervisor based on business/operational needs. Preferred Qualifications -Cleaning experience in an industrial setting. -Microfiber and green cleaning experience. -Ability to work within team and individual settings. -Ability to follow written and verbal instructions. -Ability to perform medium to heavy physical work. -Ability to attain any certifications required in some areas. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Communication: Listens to co-workers’ questions or self-identifies questions that need answering and selects an appropriate person or written source to consult to get a workable answer that can allow for progress in accomplishing the job. Customer Service: Recognizes potential problems in service, and addresses and resolves problems promptly and respectfully. Interpersonal Skills: Develops and maintains effective working relationships with others in order to encourage and support communication and teamwork. Technical Knowledge: Cleans the interior and exterior of buildings, using the appropriate cleaning solutions. Operates standard commercial floor equipment. Helps service equipment to keep it functioning properly and efficiently. Uses hot water carpet extractors to clean carpet in all academic buildings. Refinishes all tile and terrazzo floors by minor cleaning and spray buffing/waxing or stripping/waxing. Performs exterior window cleaning using heavy cleaning equipment. Safety & Health Compliance: Recognizes and follows dispenser directions to properly mix cleaning chemicals. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours 2ND SHIFT WORK HOURS : 8-hour workday schedule with primary hours within the following time frame: 3:00 pm – 12:00 midnight; Monday through Friday. Weekend work and hours other than normal schedule may be required to accomplish assigned duties. Position is subject to call in, call back or stay over on off schedule hours and weekends should emergencies occur. This position will require weekend work for sporting events and other campus events. This position is also expected to work, as needed, in the event of staffing shortages, sporting events and/or other events on campus that require Building Environmental Service needs. Supervisor assignment may be adjusted based on business/operational need. Designated as MANDATORY , this position is expected to be available for work during University emergencies, closings and adverse weather conditions. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Physical efforts include lifting and moving all types of tables, chairs, chemicals and supplies, furniture, trash and debris including snow and ice, and all cleaning equipment as required. Work can involve climbing ladders. At times, must be able to lift 50-100 pounds. Will need to be able to maneuver and set up heavy athletic equipment (ie: basketball goals, floor covers, volley ball / badminton equipment). Overall Competency Level Journey Salary Grade Equivalency 50 Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $34,321 - $35,588 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/26/2026 Closing Date 09/07/2026 Competency Level Statement If no applicants apply who meet the required competencies, then management may consider other applicants at a lower competency level. Special Instructions to Applicants Please list a minimum of 3 professional references in the application. Appalachian State University Benefits Information: https://hr.appstate.edu/hr-services/benefits Finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check. Applicant must have a valid driver’s license to be considered. Search Chair Name Jessica South Search Chair Email Southjl@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55820 Posting Number 201503036P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
