registered professional nurse is responsible for the nursing care of patients and for assisting the physician/clinician at the Mary S. Shook Student Health Services. Certified Nursing Assistant is to work with professional and supportive staff to enhance a safe and disease free/controlled work place. To provide safe, efficient, and therapeutically effective nursing care for the patient. Organize and maintain the Mary S. Shook Student Health Services facility in a clean and sanitary condition. X-Ray Technologist performs diagnostic imaging in a variety of clinical settings. Duties performed include: taking, developing, using and maintaining technical equipment effectively and/or assisting physicians during procedures. Work involves working directly with patients – preparing patients for procedures, positioning patients and providing instruction. Phlebotomist is responsible for collecting blood by performing venipuncture, finger sticks, and performing EKG’s for clinical laboratory testing and alalysis. Organization and maintian the laboratory facility and patient areas in a clean and sanitary condition. Preferred Qualifications High School Graduate with certification or license for the position in which you are applying (if required). Work Schedule/Hours Hours and times may vary depending on the position. May include some nights and weekends Number of Hours Per Week 20 or less Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range TBD--Compensation will be based on the position in which you are applying for Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 02/24/2015 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool 