    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55784": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Food Service Technician - PM",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Food Service Technician - PM Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Food Service Technician - PM Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Food Services Technician-ASU Working Title Food Service Technician - PM Location Job Category 8 Position Number 039151 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Campus Dining - Park Place Cafe - 170450 Primary Purpose of Position To serve the Appalachian community using sustainable practices, creative and intentional menus, and engaging customer service. Assisting assigned unit with any additional assigned tasks after completing primary duties. Prepare large quantities of food following Campus Dining specifications. Utilize food safety procedures and protocol following the FDA food code. Minimum Qualifications Experience in food preparation or service activities in a commercial kitchen; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. [Special Requirements may apply for individual positions such as certification requirements by Department of Correction.] Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all functions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Duties of the position may include: Maintaining all university specifications pertaining to production and service. Control proper usage and rotation of food. Ensure food quality and appearance on buffet. Alert Chef or direct supervisor to any food quality issues that could hurt culinary operations. Maintain walk-in coolers and food storage areas daily. Maintain a neat, clean, and sanitary workstation. The person selected must follow cleaning and sanitation procedures and other duties as assigned by a supervisor. Serves appropriate portion sizes determined by Unit Management Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Knowledge of methods of preparation and cooking of food in quantity lots. Knowledge of the uses of various pieces of equipment, including but not limited to steamers, steam pots, fryers, grills, slicers, and ovens. Ability to maintain high standards of personal cleanliness as well as food sanitation. The job requires attention to detail, initiative, and decision-making capabilities. Team player attitude and superior customer service skills are required. Initiative to work beyond what is requested within the unit to achieve business goals of quality and service standards. Preferred Qualifications 2+ years of related front of house food service experience. ServSafe certification should be obtained within 1 year of employment. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Campus Dining is a Sunday – Saturday, 6:00 am – 11:00 pm operation. Operations are reduced during university breaks. Employees are scheduled two days off each week based on business need. Days off may not be consecutive days off. Food Service Technician ( FST ) – PM Typical hours 3pm-12am Actual schedule time may vary. Operations are reduced during university breaks. Employees may be required to work some flex hours to support the needs of the business and/or for special campus events. Schedules will be adjusted as needed to provide coverage in these cases. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Lifting items over 50 lbs. Stooping and bending to retrieve items from ovens, shelves, etc. Sweeping and mopping area each day. Scrubbing and cleaning of all equipment daily, standing on your feet for the entire 8-hour shift. Overall Competency Level Advanced Salary Grade Equivalency Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $35,845 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/29/2026 Closing Date 09/13/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Search Chair Name Travis Pierce Search Chair Email andrewsm1@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55434 Posting Number 201503019P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53766": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Post-Doctoral / Post-Master&#39;s Resident",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Post-Doctoral / Post-Master&#39;s Resident Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Post-Doctoral / Post-Master's Resident Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following for consideration: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References with contacts Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Post-Doctoral / Post-Master's Resident Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank Position Number 090881 Department Counseling Center & Psychological Services - 315100 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Post-Doctoral / Post-Maser’s Resident contributes to the mission of the Counseling & Psychological Services Center by participating in all areas of service delivery, while gaining advanced training in university counseling center services and developing additional specialized skills. Minimum Qualifications Doctorate in Counseling or Clinical Psychology, or related field, or Master’s Degree in Counseling, Social Work, or related field, and eligibility for appropriate licensure in North Carolina. The successful candidate will be expected to make application for licensure at the start of employment and maintain any licensure status for the continuation of the appointment. License/Certification Required Doctorate in Counseling or Clinical Psychology, or related field, or Master’s Degree in Counseling, Social Work, or related field, and eligibility for appropriate licensure in North Carolina. The successful candidate will be expected to make application for licensure at the start of employment and maintain any licensure status for the continuation of the appointment. Preferred Qualifications 1. For doctoral applicants, APA approved training for both academic and internship preparation. 2. Experience in a university counseling center or demonstrated interest in providing the full range of psychological services offered by the Counseling Center. Candidates should also be committed to a proactive student affairs perspective involving an active relationship with the campus community; be team-oriented and collaborative with students, colleagues, and university staff; and have broad generalist clinical skills in assessing and intervening with a wide range of disorders, concerns, and degrees of pathology. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Duties of the position include: short-term individual, group, and couples therapy psychological assessment crisis intervention consultation outreach and psychoeducational workshops (sometimes after hours) clinical supervision and training case management as needed liaison/consultant relationships and rotating after hours emergency/crisis on call responsibilities as back-up to ProtoCall. The position includes some administrative duties and roles based on interest areas and desired areas of specialization. Specializations are flexible, based on interest, and could be in areas such as: Eating Disorders Treatment of Trauma Sports Psychology Supervision and Training Behavioral Health Consulting Multicultural Focus Administration and Leadership Or an individualized specialization may be developed. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Mon-Fri, 8:00 A.M.-5:00 P.M. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $41,400 - $43,888 Physical Demands of Position Posting Details Information Posting Date 02/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 03/16/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 08/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following for consideration: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References with contacts Search Chair Name Chris Hogan, Sammi Brown Search Chair Email hogancj@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/50768 Posting Number 201501641P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55896": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Recruiting Services Manager Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Recruiting Services Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach additional requested documents: Cover Letter and Resume. Please provide a list of 3 current and relevant references on application or attach a List of References with Contact Information: Include name, title/relationship to you, phone numbers and email addresses. Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title University Program Associate Working Title Recruiting Services Manager Location Boone NC Job Category 5 Position Number 024891 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Career Development - 305000 Primary Purpose of Position The Recruiting Services Manager ( RSM ) serves as the primary contact and manager for employers utilizing Appalachian State recruiting services. These services include but are not limited to On-Campus Recruiting, Information Sessions, Job and Internship Postings, Career Fairs, and other employer engagement opportunities. As a result, the RSM establishes and maintains relationships with employers for the purpose of providing quality on campus recruiting opportunities for students and cultivates student/alumni and employer relationships through career development opportunities. This position supervises GA, and student workers assigned to Employer Relations, and is the primary manager of content for the online career management system, known as Handshake, requiring strong technical competency; manages fair and event registrations and payments from employers; tracks and analyzes data related to events via Handshake; and supports the planning and execution of Career Development Center events and fairs . Lastly, the RSM will manage and oversee the marketing and design program for the Employer Relations unit to include both print and digital marketing. This includes expertise in graphic design, ensuring the creation of visually compelling materials that align with branding guidelines and effectively communicate key messages. The role also involves designing and managing digital and print signage, ensuring consistency and clarity in promotional and informational materials. Additionally, proficiency in social media management is required, including content creation, scheduling, audience engagement, and analytics tracking across various platforms. The ability to develop and execute strategic marketing campaigns, leveraging social media and digital tools to enhance outreach and engagement, is critical. Familiarity with marketing software, design tools (e.g., Adobe Creative Suite, Canva), and social media scheduling platforms is highly beneficial. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; or equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions The Recruiting Services Manager ( RSM ) is the primary contact and manager for employers utilizing Appalachian State’s recruiting services, which include On-Campus Recruiting, Information Sessions, Job and Internship Postings, Career Fairs, and other employer engagement opportunities. The RSM establishes and maintains relationships with employers to provide quality on-campus recruiting opportunities for students and cultivate both student/alumni and employer relationships through career development events. Responsibilities include managing all on-campus recruiting, overseeing the web-based recruiting system, coordinating employer visits and events, and collaborating with Career Counselors to identify and plan employer engagement activities. The RSM reviews, approves, and posts job and internship listings, ensures smooth interview scheduling for students and employers, and troubleshoots issues with the online career management system, Handshake. Additionally, the RSM supervises student workers assigned to Employer Relations and is responsible for coordinating campus-wide career events, such as career fairs and information sessions, including the development and administration of event evaluations. The RSM also manages the marketing and design program for Employer Relations, which includes creating and managing digital and print signage to ensure consistent branding and effective communication. Proficiency in graphic design, social media management, and the ability to develop strategic marketing campaigns is essential. The role requires strong skills in content creation, audience engagement, scheduling, and tracking analytics across platforms. Familiarity with marketing software and design tools such as Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, and social media scheduling platforms is highly beneficial. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position The Recruiting Services Manager coordinates technical processing functions within Recruitment Program and Registration Management, often serving as the process and procedural expert. This role oversees the day-to-day operations of recruiting services, ensuring seamless program execution by planning and organizing activities, interpreting policies and procedures, and providing high-quality customer service to students, employers, and other stakeholders. The position requires extensive knowledge of recruitment processes, career services operations, and related information technology systems. Serving as the primary point of contact for the program, the Recruiting Services Manager is responsible for problem-solving procedural issues, managing business accounts and records, and facilitating employer engagement efforts. Additionally, this role may involve supervising student employees, assisting with career fairs and recruiting events, and coordinating transactional services to support the overall success of the program. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position: Customer service-minded individual; proven strengths in providing excellent public service and compassion necessary to work with students seeking jobs and internships as well as the employers and intern hosts eager to reach the students and faculty of Appalachian State University. Reliable and self-directed with the ability to supervise staff and processes; Values aligned with the mission of the Career Development Center and Academic Affairs; Demonstrated proficiency with databases/computer information systems/web-based communications; Ability to adapt and adjust to technology changes and/or feature enhancements as well as to recommend those; Strong working knowledge of both print and digital marketing is essential to include graphic design, digital & print signage, social media management is required; Possess excellent organizational skills including event management; Balance multiple projects and set program priorities effectively; Manage frequent interruptions and simultaneously demonstrate strong communication skills; Exercise integrity, confidentiality, sensitivity, and discretion in interpreting and applying recruitment policies and procedures; Assessment skills to review employer relations policies and make recommendations for needed changes; General knowledge of budget management. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with Canva, Adobe InDesign/Creative Suite, Technology, social media, and database experience is desired. Experience with supervision is a plus. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Program/Project Administration: Ability to administer and manage a component of a broad program or project. Ability to maintain program/project databases, schedules and reports. Ability to ensure accuracy of data. Ability to perform related administrative duties including coordination with other work units. Ability to research funding opportunities. Ability to assist in grant writing and contract proposal development. Professional Knowledge: Knowledge of program policies and procedures and technology related to assigned program area(s). Ability to apply and interpret them for clients while providing services. Knowledge of program/service guidelines demonstrated by the ability to identify, evaluate, and resolve recurring work issues. Knowledge of State and federal laws and/or regulations in assigned program area(s). Ability to determine the correct or most appropriate course(s) of action. Communication & Marketing: Ability to establish and maintain productive and collaborative professional work relationships with clients and respond to questions within policy and procedure guidelines in assigned area(s). Ability to use concepts and language that are easy for others to understand. Ability to use active listening to assure mutual understanding through shared information and viewpoints. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday-Friday; 8:00 am-5:00 pm Evenings, early mornings, and weekends in preparation for campus-wide career events (approximately 8-10 instances a year). Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position Ability to move and transport light loads of career event material. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Overall Competency Level Advanced Salary Grade Equivalency GN09 Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $47,000 - $49,000 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date 09/30/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach additional requested documents: Cover Letter and Resume. Please provide a list of 3 current and relevant references on application or attach a List of References with Contact Information: Include name, title/relationship to you, phone numbers and email addresses. Search Chair Name Chad Leder Search Chair Email ledercr@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55693 Posting Number 201503033P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe which social media platforms you have experience navigating and/or managing. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any experience in Event Planning? Yes No * Do you have a thorough knowledge of design techniques including Indesign, Photoshop, and Illustrator? Yes No * This job requires a great deal of verbal and written communication skills. Please describe your education and/or experience that has prepared you for communicating detailed information to a variety of people. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/43051": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Graphic Design Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Graphic Design Adjunct Instructor Pool Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Graphic Design Adjunct Instructor Pool Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter — the letter should include a list of which Graphic Design courses you would be qualiﬁed to teach and what your approach to those courses would be. Curriculum vitae List of references with contact information Sample teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, previous teaching evaluations) are encouraged but not required upon initial application. Ofﬁcial transcripts will be required at a later stage of hire consideration. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Graphic Design Adjunct Instructor Pool Department Art - 265050 Location Boone, NC Position Number 018863 Description of Department The Department of Art is accredited by NASAD and has 47 full-time faculty members, over 20 part-time faculty members, over 800 undergraduate majors and offers the following degrees: BFAs in Art Education, Graphic Design, Photography with concentrations in Commercial and Fine Art, and Studio Art; a BA in Art & Visual Culture with concentrations in Art History, Art Management and Studio Art; and a BS in Graphic Communications Management with concentrations in Cross Media Production and Print/Packaging Production. The Department of Art typically offers a range of travel opportunities including trips to the university’s New York Loft and has offered study abroad trips to China, Costa Rica, Cuba, Italy, Japan, the Netherlands, Scotland, Spain, and Taiwan. Additional information about the department, the university, and the surrounding area can be found at art.appstate.edu. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or related discipline or BFA in Graphic Design with extensive professional experience. Essential Job Functions The Department of Art seeks to hire multiple adjunct instructors for various courses in graphic design for Spring 2024 and the academic year 2024-25. Instruction may be face-to-face or online, depending on need. Essential job functions include course preparation and delivery, grading, student engagement, and weekly ofﬁce hours. Instructors are expected to submit materials for departmental and/or General Education assessment as requested by the department chair. Courses taught may include: ART 1102: Introduction to Graphic Design ART 2102: Typography I ART 3102: Typography II ART 3202: Interaction Design I ART 3302: Sign, Symbol, Image ART 4102: Typography III ART 3602: Special Topics in Graphic Design Other courses depending on department need and instructor expertise are welcome. Applicants may also propose a topic not currently included among those listed in the course catalog (please see the list of courses for Graphic Design ). Preferred Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or related discipline Relevant teaching experience Experience teaching online asynchronous courses Number of Hours Per Week Variable Number of Months per Year 9 Hiring Range Commensurate with qualifications and equity Posting Details Posting Date 11/01/2023 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire 01/16/2024 Evaluation of Applications Begins 11/01/2023 Search Chair Name Mark Nystrom Search Chair Email nystromml@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter — the letter should include a list of which Graphic Design courses you would be qualiﬁed to teach and what your approach to those courses would be. Curriculum vitae List of references with contact information Sample teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, previous teaching evaluations) are encouraged but not required upon initial application. Ofﬁcial transcripts will be required at a later stage of hire consideration. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which of the following best describes your interest and experience teaching fully online courses? I am not interested in teaching online courses I am interested in teaching online courses, but I have no previous experience. I have previous experience teaching online courses and would be interested in teaching online for App State Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Link to Portfolio Sample Syllabus Evidence of Teaching Teaching Evaluations & Peer Reviews Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
