    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55530": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences)",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences) Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 018531 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Psychology - 250800 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Psychology or a related field by the starting date. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) Prefer expertise in Personality and Individual Differences. The area of specialization within Personality Psychology is open. Applicants whose primary area of specialization is outside Personality will be considered, as long as they demonstrate knowledge of and competence in the field of Personality Psychology. License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department has 43 full-time faculty members (33 tenure-track) with graduate programs in Clinical, Psychological Science, Industrial-Organizational and Human Resource Management, and School Psychology. There are more than 1400 undergraduate majors and nearly 100 full-time graduate students. Additional information about the Department of Psychology is located on the Psychology Department website . Essential Duties and Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to teach an undergraduate course in Personality and Individual Differences, in addition to other courses, according to need and/or interest (e.g., Psychology of Personality, Personality Laboratory, Contemporary Issues in Psychology). The successful candidate will be expected to establish a program of empirical research, including peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and external grant applications. They will also be expected to involve undergraduate and graduate students in their research programs and may affiliate with any of the Department’s four graduate programs. Preference will be given to candidates with a commitment to undergraduate education and the ability to involve undergraduate and graduate students in their program of research. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester, which might include a combination of undergraduate and graduate courses. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 07/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: A cover letter addressing the candidate’s qualifications for the Assistant Professor position in Personality and Individual Differences A Curriculum Vita Unofficial Graduate Transcripts A statement of teaching philosophy, interests, and evidence of teaching effectiveness that includes which courses from the Undergraduate Psychology Bulletin you would be able to teach A statement of research interests and research plans for the next 3 years A list of three professional References with contact information. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later date. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 08/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Chris Dickinson Search Chair Email dickinsonca@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54387 Posting Number FA00585P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54899": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor, Cluster Hires in Biology: Integrative Biology",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor, Cluster Hires in Biology: Integrative Biology Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor, Cluster Hires in Biology: Integrative Biology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, applications must include: A cover letter Curriculum vitae Teaching statement Statement of research interests The names and contact information (including e-mail) of three referees familiar with the applicant’s teaching and/or scholarship. Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor, Cluster Hires in Biology: Integrative Biology Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 016901, 005241 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Biology - 250100 Working Location (City, State) Boone, North Carolina Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications A PhD in Biology or related field with postdoctoral experience. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) The Department of Biology at Appalachian State University is excited to announce a cluster hiring to enhance our research and teaching in the Integrative Biology concentration. We invite applications for two tenure-track positions at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in Fall 2027. We seek applicants who take an integrative approach to investigating interactions between organisms and their changing environments in the following areas: Research that employs integrative techniques to address evolutionary or ecological questions related to host-pathogen/symbiont interactions, disease ecology, quantifying the impact of climate change on species interactions, or quantifying differing responses to change across organismal lineages. We intend to hire one applicant who addresses one or more of these questions in plants and one in animals. We are particularly interested in candidates who complement the current departmental strengths. Teaching responsibilities could include: Evolution, Ecology, Global Change Ecology, Plant Physiology, and rotate into the first-year biology sequence. The successful candidates will have the opportunity to develop integrative courses in their area of specialty. License/Certification Required None Required. Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Biology at Appalachian State University is a community of 44 faculty who are active in teaching and research, along with a support staff of 6 technicians and 3 administrators. We strive to maintain a faculty with diverse research interests, ranging from molecules to organisms to landscapes. The department currently has approximately 950 Biology majors and 70 graduate students. We provide instruction in biology through classroom and laboratory interactions, undergraduate and graduate laboratory research experiences, seminars, professional development programs, and career advising through courses and faculty interactions. Faculty typically teach 3 courses per semester (mixture of lectures and labs). Departmental and university service includes, but is not limited to, undergraduate advising, curriculum development, and assessment. The Department of Biology manages and provides access to a research greenhouse , a 67 acre nature preserve on campus, an off campus 250 acre field site , I.W. Carpenter Jr. Herbarium , and App State Zoological Collections. The institution and department have facilities to support the use of cutting-edge molecular techniques, including instrumentation for flow cytometry, gel imaging, cell culture, and Illumina sequencing. The Rankin Science Building is home to the William and Ruth Dewel Microscopy Facility , which provides infrastructure for epifluorescence, confocal, scanning electron, and transmission electron microscopy, as well as sample preparation. The department and university support new faculty through a comprehensive Faculty Mentoring Program and Center for Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Student Success . The mechanisms include peer writing circles, pedagogical workshops, and faculty mentoring. Appalachian State University, in North Carolina’s Blue Ridge Mountains, prepares students to lead purposeful lives as global citizens who understand and engage their responsibilities in creating a sustainable future for all. The transformational Appalachian experience promotes a spirit of inclusion that brings people together in inspiring ways to acquire and create knowledge, to grow holistically, to act with passion and determination, and embrace diversity and difference. As one of 17 campuses in the University of North Carolina system, Appalachian State enrolls over 21,000 students, and offers more than 150 undergraduate and 80 graduate majors. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will include required and elective courses in the candidate’s area of expertise, and participation in the Introductory Biology sequence for majors. The successful candidates are expected to develop a research program that is competitive for external funding and involves undergraduate and master’s students. Applicants must be able to teach face-to-face and online with students in large lecture and small discussion formats, and teach in laboratory settings with individual students and small student groups. Faculty will also be expected to meet with students, and advisees to provide guidance regarding their academic progress. Faculty are additionally expected to meet with colleagues to provide discussion and insight regarding academics and/or the function, maintenance and future of the Department, College and University. Meetings with students and/or colleagues may occur in face-to-face or online, either in small or large group settings. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position Typical physical demands of a professional position at the university. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/02/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: No ABD consideration (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Applications must include (i) a cover letter that includes information on how the applicant’s research and teaching interests will complement and/or synergize with current departmental offerings (2 pages max), (ii) a curriculum vitae, (iii) a research statement that highlights short-term and long-term goals and the involvement of undergraduate and master’s student researchers (3 pages max), (iv) a teaching statement that includes philosophy, specific interests and experience, strategies for managing a 3-3 teaching load, and mentorship strategies (3 pages max), and (v) the contact information for 3 references (name, address, telephone, email). UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 06/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 08/31/2026 Search Chair Name Clare Scott Chialvo, Lynn Siefferman Search Chair Email chialvoch@appstate.edu, sieffermanlm@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54803 Posting Number FA00353P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research Interests Statement on Teaching & Mentoring Philosophy List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56007": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Financial Aid Advisor/Reception Representative Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Financial Aid Advisor/Reception Representative Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the required documents: Cover Letter Resume List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application or attach a List of References with Contact Information Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Administrative Support Specialist-OSP Working Title Financial Aid Advisor/Reception Representative Location Boone, North Carolina Job Category 6 Position Number 091561 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Enrollment Mgt - Office of Student Financial Aid & University Scholarships - 240500 Primary Purpose of Position This position will be the primary staff assistant to a department or program manager. The position will be at the front line of greeting, referring, and assisting visitors, students, parents, staff, and others for the Office of Financial Aid & University Scholarships. This position will manage data collection and analysis, conduct research, and reconcile financial or informational records to ensure accuracy. Preparation of technical reports and the composition of professional correspondence, including memos, emails, and letters. Administrative responsibilities include comprehensive records management, use of advanced office technology, and maintenance of departmental filing systems, including compiling records, organizing and maintaining files, and posting information. Prompt email correspondence and daily mail distribution. Photocopying and scanning of documents. This position will moderate and facilitate the Financial Aid Walk-in Zoom hours and compile the associated reporting information. Scheduling and assisting the department or program manager with work-study students’ calendars, possible review or approval of payroll, and assisting and participating in outreach events, including but not limited to communication to students and parents on requirements and deadlines, and other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Graduation from high school and one year of related office experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all positions. Diplomas or degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions The Financial Aid Advisor/Reception Representative duties include creating a welcoming environment for students and families as they arrive in the office, managing front-line student workers, ensuring the front desk is staffed, fielding phone calls and emails from students and parents, diagnosing problems and concerns based on knowledge of financial aid application and eligibility processes, providing basic advising and resolution, discerning and appropriately routing complex and higher-level inquiries and situations, using an open-ticket system to track and route inquiries, and researching systems and resources as appropriate. Duties also include identifying unique concerns and trends, and advising management. Additional administrative support may be required in other functional areas within the office, including call center backup, digital imaging, and other processing tasks. The Financial Aid Advisor/Reception Representative is responsible for accurately and professionally answering first-line financial aid application and eligibility questions in a high-volume, fast-paced customer contact center. Responses must follow federal, state, and institutional rules and regulations and align with training and management guidelines. The position requires computer proficiency, strong keyboarding skills, excellent oral and written communication skills, strong analytical skills and attention to detail, use of good judgment and tact, and a positive, helpful customer orientation. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position The position requires computer proficiency, strong keyboarding skills, excellent oral and written communication skills, strong analytical skills and attention to detail, use of good judgment and tact, and a positive, helpful customer orientation. Considerable knowledge of services, policies and procedures related to a program or area of specialization. Ability to demonstrate and apply this knowledge in performance of administrative tasks; ability to explain and interpret information to clients/customers and staff. Considerable knowledge of program policies, procedures and information systems in order to communicate and process information. Ability to compile, assimilate and organize both printed and electronic information; ability to apply knowledge of data collection, storage, organization, manipulation and/or analysis of data. Ability to utilize office equipment and other relevant technology (software and systems) to meet organizational needs. Ability to identify and understand issues, problems, and opportunities; use effective approaches for choosing a course of action or developing appropriate solutions. Ability to clearly convey information and ideas through a variety of media to individuals or groups. Ability to communicate effectively (written and oral) Preferred Qualifications Experience with database software such as Banner Experience working with students or in higher education Experience working with scanning software Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Information/Records Administration: Coordinates varied records processing activities requiring the application and some interpretation of agency procedures, policies, laws, and regulations. Reviews information for completeness and accuracy using multiple guidelines. Knowledge-Program: Program knowledge includes acceptable interpretations, applications, and allowable exceptions of written policies and procedures. Requires knowledge of organizational structure, functions, and services, programs, office procedures and practices. Communication-Verbal: Presents ideas in a clear, concise, organized manner. Explains and interprets programs, policies and procedures to meet the specific needs of staff and clients. Advises program staff/clients in all matters related to program operations. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday through Friday, 8:00-5:00 pm Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Overall Competency Level Journey Salary Grade Equivalency Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $38,127-$40,842 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date 09/20/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the required documents: Cover Letter Resume List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application or attach a List of References with Contact Information Search Chair Name Alison Rabil Search Chair Email rabila1@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56006 Posting Number 201503051P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/51848": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Catering Cook Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Catering Cook Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following documents: Resume List of References with contact information Cover Letter/Letter of Interest (optional) Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Catering Cook Location Boone, NC Position Number N32305 Department Catering Kitchen - 1703CC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications 2 years of experience in food preparation or service activities in a commercial kitchen; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Grandview Catering & Events provides handcrafted fare and unique experiences brought to life by culinary and event professionals inspired by the latest trends and classic comforts. We focus on attention to detail, quality ingredients and sustainable practices with exceptional customer service. We proudly serve Appalachian State University campuses as well as off-site events for university affiliated businesses, community members and alumni. We’re looking for a team-oriented and driven individual to hit the ground running and join our growing team and an influx of special event bookings. The successful candidate will work with others to ensure the highest quality of food is prepared and ready to be served within the appropriate time frame. Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Cooking and assisting in the food production for catered events. Help prepare kitchen area, work spaces and event set ups for food preparation and service Working alongside the catering sous chef and executive catering chef, as well as student staff Willingness to step in as needed to assist all back of house positions including other cooks, pastry chef, sous chef, dishwasher, set up crew and student staff. Following menu standards, standardized specifications, and ServSafe protocol. Monitoring the quality of the product and service provided Understanding of safe food handling policies and procedures Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines during each shift Maintain open and frequent communication team members and supervisor regarding event status, questions, concerns and new ideas Form positive working relationships with coworkers while remaining professional and respectful at all times Work with the entire Grandview team on other duties as assigned Preferred Qualifications 2+ years of related experience Culinary School/ ACF Certification. Obtain ServSafe certification within 1 year of employment Time management and organizational skills Work Schedule/Hours Schedule varies depending on business needs Catering employees are required to work special events including, but not limited to, home football games, University commencement, other large scale events Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $16.00-19.00 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/14/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following documents: Resume List of References with contact information Cover Letter/Letter of Interest (optional) Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/51789 Posting Number 201500987P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letter of Recommendation (1st doc) List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55798": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Technical Assistance Lead (2 Vacancies), Rural Health Transformation Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Technical Assistance Lead (2 Vacancies), Rural Health Transformation Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a grant-funded position contingent upon final contract/subaward execution, continued funding, satisfactory performance, and University approval. Final classification, salary range, reporting line, and posting language are subject to App State Human Resources review. Applicants should submit a resume, cover letter/letter of interest, and a list of three professional references with contact information. Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Technical Assistance Lead (2 Vacancies), Rural Health Transformation Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank N/A Position Number 0A1121 Department Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness - 273600 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Technical Assistance Specialist provides specialized career services and workforce pathway support to students and trainees preparing for rural health careers. The position works with employers, training sites, educational programs, and community partners to develop experiential learning and work-based opportunities, assess site readiness, address placement barriers, and support successful transitions from education and training into rural employment. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in career services, higher education, counseling, workforce development, education, public health, health sciences, social work, healthcare administration, human resources, or a related field. At least three years of professional experience in career services, employer engagement, workforce pathway development, experiential or community-engaged learning, internships, apprenticeships, clinical or field placements, healthcare or public health workforce, or student and trainee services. Experience working directly with students or trainees and external employers, healthcare providers, public health agencies, community-based organizations, supervisors, preceptors, or training sites. Demonstrated advising, facilitation, consultation, problem-solving, writing, training, data interpretation, and relationship-management skills. License/Certification Required No license or certification is required. Project management, workforce development, public health, clinical, or related certifications may be preferred where applicable. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field. Experience in rural health, behavioral health, public health, clinical education, apprenticeships, work-based learning, community-engaged learning, rural residency, service learning, or academic-practice partnerships. Experience helping employers, healthcare providers, public health agencies, community organizations, or training sites establish internships, placements, rotations, fellowships, apprenticeships, or early-career employment opportunities. Experience evaluating career-services, experiential-learning, placement, transition-to-employment, or workforce-retention outcomes. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Develop rural health career pathways and employer or training-site networks. Work with educational programs, healthcare employers, public health agencies, behavioral health providers, emergency services, community organizations, and training sites to define pathways, participant roles, learning experiences, supervision, and progression from education into rural employment. Provide specialized career guidance and participant preparation. Assess interests, preparation, and career goals; explain pathway, placement, and applicable service-commitment requirements; support career-readiness activities; and help students and trainees navigate Scholars, Fellows, apprenticeships, paid work-based learning, clinical and field placements, rural rotations, community-based experiences, and related programs. Assess and strengthen employer and training-site readiness. Review participant roles, learning objectives, supervision and preceptor structures, onboarding, confidentiality, safety, technology, documentation, communication, participant supports, and placement workflows; provide technical assistance; and recommend changes that improve experience quality and site capacity. Coordinate participant-site matching, experiential learning, and placement follow-through. Work with participants, academic programs, employers, providers, and community sites to identify appropriate opportunities, confirm requirements, support onboarding, monitor progress, resolve barriers, and strengthen transition from the experience into rural employment. Develop and deliver career-services resources, training, and partner support. Create pathway maps, employer and supervisor guides, placement tools, orientation materials, training sessions, career-connected project resources, and other supports tailored to participant and site needs. Monitor outcomes and coordinate regional follow-up. Track participant, employer, site, placement, completion, credential, transition-to-employment, and retention outcomes; gather feedback; identify recurring barriers; maintain required documentation; coordinate with App State, Vaya, AHEC , public health anchors, and other partners; and recommend improvements. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Mon-Fri, 8:00-5:00 pm Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $70,000 Physical Demands of Position This position primarily involves office and computer-based work, including sitting, typing, reading, analysis, virtual meetings, advising, facilitation, and communication. Regular travel to campuses, employers, provider and community sites, training sites, and regional meetings is required. Occasional lifting or transport of materials up to 20 pounds may be required. Individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/25/2026 Closing Date 09/08/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/09/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 09/21/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants This is a grant-funded position contingent upon final contract/subaward execution, continued funding, satisfactory performance, and University approval. Final classification, salary range, reporting line, and posting language are subject to App State Human Resources review. Applicants should submit a resume, cover letter/letter of interest, and a list of three professional references with contact information. Search Chair Name Alex F. Howard Search Chair Email howardaf@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55797 Posting Number 201501833P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55620": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Power Line Tech II Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Power Line Tech II Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. List a minimum of 3 professional references on application. All candidates hired will be required to complete some (based on experience level) or all portions of NC and NRLP apprenticeship program through New River Light & Power to demonstrate competency. Also may complete the program to obtain DoL credentials after completion of required OJT hours. CDL Class B will be required within 6 months of hire. Candidate will be asked to demonstrate physical and basic technical abilities as part of the interview and consideration process. Applicants have the option (but are not required) to attach a Resume, Cover Letter, or Letter of Recommendation Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title High Voltage Distribution Specialist Working Title Power Line Tech II Location Boone, NC Job Category 7 Position Number 052611 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department New River Light and Power Co - 170600 Primary Purpose of Position Work in this class involves the construction, maintenance, and repair of high-voltage underground and overhead primary and secondary electric distribution lines. Install and maintain New River Light and Power’s fiber-optic network. Minimum Qualifications Completion of high school and six months of electrical experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Special Note: Maintains required certifications. Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all positions. License/Certification Required CDL is required within 6 months of hire date Essential Job Functions This position is responsible for working with live high voltage conductors, maintenance of electrical equipment, installation of underground power lines, and the repair of overhead lines and poles. Will install and maintain NRLP’s fiber optic network cables. Climbing, hand work, digging, heavy lifting, and all weather work is required. This position must be able to train and assist less experienced “B” line workers with the proper repair of live high and low voltage lines. This position must be familiar in the use of various powered equipment and safety techniques including; climbing gear, bucket/digger trucks, excavators, high voltage gloves, and hoses. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Knowledge, skills, and abilities that involve the construction, maintenance, and repair of high-voltage underground and overhead primary and secondary electric distribution lines. Applies thorough knowledge of all applicable codes and methods of installation and repair Read and interpret schematics drawing and recommend corrective actions. Must have the ability to operate University owned vehicles with valid driver’s license. Demonstrates journeyman level skills and knowledge, with ability to complete both physical and technical duties. Must live or relocate to within approximately 20 minute commute of Boone within 90 days of hire. Preferred Qualifications High school graduate. Credentials from an Electrical Utility Lineman School Program and 4 years of electrical Lineworker related work experience or 5 years of electrical Lineworker related work experience. Lives within 20 minutes of Boone, NC. Holds DoL Journeyman credentials. Holds CDL Class B license. AS A MINIMUM Completion of high school and 4-year minimum of recent high voltage electrical experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Must have knowledge of electric power distribution lines, National Electric Safety Code, electrical theory, system service rules and regulations and pertinent policies and practices. Ability to safely work on energized and de‑energized lines. Ability to lift more than 50 lbs. Ability to climb poles, work at heights, and perform strenuous physical tasks in various weather conditions. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Knowledge – Technical: 1. Applies thorough knowledge of construction, installation and maintenance of applicable systems, standard practices, materials, and techniques involved in the construction of primary and secondary overhead and underground distribution facilities. 2. Applies thorough knowledge of all applicable codes and methods of installation and repair; Read and interpret schematics drawing and recommend corrective actions. Equipment Operation: Must have thorough knowledge and skill in the operation and use of applicable equipment, tool and vehicle in the operation, construction, maintenance and repair of high-voltage primary and secondary overhead and underground distribution facilities, in order to instruct lower-level lineman and trainees. Leadership: Functions in a supervisory role for direct reports. May perform as a lead for more complex operation. Participates in making work assignments and ensuring compliance with standards, career development of employees, and performance evaluation. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Mon-Fri, 7:00-4:00 pm Some call back and after hours required. Designated as MANDATORY , this position is expected to be available for work during NRLP /University emergencies, closings, adverse weather conditions, and other department defined events. Will be part of after hours on call response rotation. Must live or relocate to within approximately 20 minute commute of Boone within 90 days of hire. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Employee must be physically able to perform the duties of the job. Candidate will be asked to demonstrate physical abilities as part of the interview and consideration process. A physical assessment and skills test will be administered to finalists who qualify. Overall Competency Level Advanced Salary Grade Equivalency Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $69,878 - $90,000 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 04/22/2026 Closing Date 12/28/2026 Competency Level Statement If no applicants apply who meet the required competencies, then management may consider other applicants at a lower competency level. Special Instructions to Applicants List a minimum of 3 professional references on application. All candidates hired will be required to complete some (based on experience level) or all portions of NC and NRLP apprenticeship program through New River Light & Power to demonstrate competency. Also may complete the program to obtain DoL credentials after completion of required OJT hours. CDL Class B will be required within 6 months of hire. Candidate will be asked to demonstrate physical and basic technical abilities as part of the interview and consideration process. Applicants have the option (but are not required) to attach a Resume, Cover Letter, or Letter of Recommendation Search Chair Name Cory Fetters Search Chair Email fettersca@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53567 Posting Number 201502953P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letter of Recommendation (1st doc) Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53978": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Career &amp; Technical Education Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Career &amp; Technical Education Adjunct Instructor Pool Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Career & Technical Education Adjunct Instructor Pool Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must upload: 1. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest 2. Curriculum Vitae – current 3. List of References with Contact Information – names, email addresses, and telephone contact information for three professional references 4. A copy of graduate transcripts (unofficial/uncertified) Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Career & Technical Education Adjunct Instructor Pool Department Media, Career Studies, and Leadership Development - 260750 Location Boone or Hickory Campus, or online/remote Position Number 045958 Description of Department The Department of Media, Career Studies, and Leadership Development is one of five departments in the Reich College of Education, offering programs that prepare students for employment in a wide variety of teaching, administrative, and service roles, as well as employment or career advancement in business and industry. The department includes programs in Career and Technical Education; Organizational Leadership & Learning; Media, Technology and Learning Design; Library Science; International Leadership; and School Administration. The department serves students at the main campus in Boone and the new Hickory campus, in addition to App State Online students. The Career and Technical Education ( CTE ) Program at Appalachian State University is comprised of seven areas of concentration, including six teaching concentrations. Each teaching concentration provides students with the opportunity to focus on middle and high school teaching while developing a greater depth of knowledge in a specific area of Career and Technical Education ( CTE ). Through experiential learning and relevant projects, students are challenged to develop a comprehensive knowledge base. Partnerships with programs across campus give CTE students the opportunity to work with discipline-specific experts while still learning the art of teaching. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Career & Technical Education, Education, or a related discipline is required. Related disciplines may include fields aligned with CTE career pathways (e.g., business, communications, FCS , agriculture, health sciences, technology, computer science, or trade & industry), or candidates may demonstrate exceptional professional experience. Essential Job Functions Teaching Extensive teaching in on-campus environments as well as hybrid and online courses. Develop and deliver undergraduate and graduate courses related to business communications (personal finance), cross-cultural communications, data and assessment, learning analytics, leadership, and professional development. Create and update curriculum materials to reflect advancements in the field. Foster a welcoming and engaging learning environment that encourages critical thinking and creativity. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Preferred Qualifications N/A Number of Hours Per Week 10 Number of Months per Year 5 Hiring Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Posting Details Posting Date 04/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire Evaluation of Applications Begins 04/23/2026 Search Chair Name Tempestt Adams Search Chair Email adamstr2@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must upload: 1. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest 2. Curriculum Vitae – current 3. List of References with Contact Information – names, email addresses, and telephone contact information for three professional references 4. A copy of graduate transcripts (unofficial/uncertified) UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Resume Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
