    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55919": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | RIEEE Program Assistant",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | RIEEE Program Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources RIEEE Program Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit resume, cover letter and 3 professional references Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title RIEEE Program Assistant Location Boone, NC Position Number N07570 Department Res Inst Energy, Environ & Economic - 230000 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; or equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Strong organizational and multitasking skills. Demonstrated knowledge of or experience in administrative and/or business operations functions. Proficient with Google Suite. Effective communication and teamwork abilities. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Position Summary: The Program Assistant provides essential administrative, financial, and operational support to the Research Institute for Environment, Energy, and Economics ( RIEEE ) and its affiliated centers. RIEEE works with faculty partners across campus to pursue and manage grant funding and related programming. Working under the direction of the Business Operations Manager, this role ensures the smooth execution of business operations, financial transactions, office management, and event and workshop logistics. The Program Assistant also plays a key role in streamlining administrative processes, generating data for reports, and overseeing student office support. Key Responsibilities: Administrative and Business Operations Support The Program Assistant plays a vital role in supporting the daily business operations of RIEEE and its affiliated centers by assisting with: Processing contracts, invoices, and deposits, ensuring timely payments and financial compliance. Managing PCard reconciliations, travel approvals and reimbursements, and various purchasing activities. Supporting time and leave reporting and payroll processes for institute and center employees. Organizing and generating data for reports to assist the Business Operations Manager with budget tracking and fund management. Program and Event Coordination The Program Assistant supports the planning and execution of workshops, conferences, and events hosted by RIEEE , its affiliated centers, and faculty partners. Responsibilities include: Assisting with event logistics, registration, and scheduling to ensure smooth execution. Coordinating internal reporting processes, including event attendance and research impact metrics. Supporting communications efforts by curating email distribution lists, drafting email communications and event announcements for dissemination, updating website content, and formatting and/or printing outreach materials. Monitoring and supervising the Student Office Assistant, ensuring task completion and operational efficiency. Office Management The Program Assistant ensures efficient operation and organization of RIEEE’s office space by: Procuring, organizing, and maintaining office supplies and equipment, ensuring availability for staff and faculty. Coordinating the allocation and organization of office spaces, assisting with office moves, workspace assignments, and resource distribution. Tracking and maintaining fixed assets, processing work orders, and ensuring office operations run efficiently. Managing the scheduling and use of shared spaces, including conference rooms, meeting areas, and common workspaces to optimize accessibility and efficiency. Preferred Qualifications Experience in academic, research, and/or grants management environments. Experience with Banner Finance, Yo-Mart, and other platforms used for business operations at Appalachian State Experience supervising student employees. Familiarity with budget reporting processes. Work Schedule/Hours Flexible, with regular schedule during normal business hours; occasional evening and weekend work and travel required. Number of Hours Per Week 30-40 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position An individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $18.00 - $22.00 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date 09/17/2026 Open Until Filled No Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Submit resume, cover letter and 3 professional references Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55918 Posting Number 201501150P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/46009": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Part Time Special Faculty of Supply Chain Management - Hickory Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Part Time Special Faculty of Supply Chain Management - Hickory Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter ● CV ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Part Time Special Faculty of Supply Chain Management - Hickory Department Marketing & Supply Chain Mgmt (SCM) - 255350 Location Hickory, NC Position Number 018872 Description of Department Marketing & Supply Chain Management is currently the largest department (in terms of undergraduate degree seeking students) of six departments within the John A. Walker College of Business. Business students may choose from three marketing concentrations – General Marketing, Digital Marketing, or Professional Selling. The department also offers minors in professional selling (for business majors), sales (for non-business majors), and general marketing (for non-business majors). Additionally, business students can earn a Supply Chain Management major or minor. Graduate level courses are offered in the MBA / MS in Analytics program. This position will serve Appalachian State’s new campus in Hickory, N.C. The Marketing & Supply Chain Management Department consists of 16 tenured/ tenure track and 11 adjunct faculty members. The Walker College of Business is one of the largest public business schools for undergraduate students in the University of North Carolina system. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Business, Supply Chain Management, or closely related field. Essential Job Functions The person who fills this position will be expected to provide instruction primarily in Principles of Supply Chain Management, Global Supply Chain and Logistics, Strategic Procurement and Global Sourcing, and Operations Management. Instructional duties will include a teaching load of up to six credit hours per semester and participation in curriculum development. In addition to instructional duties faculty members will be expected to contribute to service activities such as alumni relations, participation in student recruiting activities, and other departmental activities. Preferred Qualifications The department is especially interested in candidates with teaching interests in one or more of the following areas – Supply Chain Management, Operations Management, Logistics, and/or Procurement. Number of Hours Per Week TBD - Part Time, Semester to Semester Number of Months per Year 9 Hiring Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Posting Details Posting Date 05/13/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire Evaluation of Applications Begins 05/13/2024 Search Chair Name Stephanie J. Lawson Search Chair Email lawsonsj1@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter ● CV ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54996": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Cell Biology",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Cell Biology Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor of Cell Biology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor of Cell Biology Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 062031 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Biology - 250100 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in Biology or related field postdoctoral experience Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) The Department of Biology at Appalachian State University seeks to fill a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor to start in the fall semester of 2027. Successful applicants will have a commitment to teaching and research at a master’s degree granting institution. They will have a PhD and postdoctoral experience, training in any subdiscipline of eukaryotic cell biology, and a research program that addresses fundamental principles of life at the cellular and molecular levels. In addition, they will teach a sophomore-level Cell Biology course, develop an advanced course in the applicant’s area of expertise, and may periodically participate in the first-year biology sequence. We seek colleagues who are enthusiastic about using research to enhance undergraduate and graduate education and who will develop a research program that is competitive for external funding. Applicants with research and teaching interests that complement or synergize with existing research programs and curriculum within the department and who use model systems that do not require extensive use of vivarium facilities are especially encouraged to apply. License/Certification Required None Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Biology at Appalachian State University is a community of 44 faculty who are active in teaching and research, along with a support staff of 6 technicians and 3 administrators. We strive to maintain a faculty with diverse research interests, ranging from molecules to organisms to landscapes. The department currently has approximately 950 Biology majors and 70 graduate students. We provide instruction in biology through classroom and laboratory interactions, undergraduate and graduate laboratory research experiences, seminars, professional development programs, and career advising through courses and faculty interactions. Faculty typically teach 3 courses per semester (mixture of lectures and labs). Departmental and university service includes, but is not limited to, undergraduate advising, curriculum development, and assessment. The institution and department have facilities to support cutting-edge cellular and molecular research. The Rankin Science Building is home to the William and Ruth Dewel Microscopy Facility , which provides infrastructure for epifluorescence, confocal, scanning electron, and transmission electron microscopy, as well as sample preparation. The Department of Biology also houses a shared research space and instrumentation core for flow cytometry, gel imaging, cell culture, and Illumina sequencing, and it manages and provides access to a research greenhouse , nature preserve , and field site . The department and university support new faculty through a comprehensive Faculty Mentoring Program and Center for Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Student Success . The mechanisms include peer writing circles, pedagogical workshops, and faculty mentoring. Essential Duties and Responsibilities We seek colleagues who are enthusiastic about using research to enhance undergraduate and graduate education and are expected to develop a research program that is competitive for external funding. Applicants with research and teaching interests that complement or synergize with existing research programs and curriculum within the department are especially encouraged to apply. Teaching responsibilities will include a sophomore-level Cell Biology course, periodic participation in the first-year biology sequence, and the eventual development of an advanced course in the applicant’s area of expertise. Departmental and university service includes, but is not limited to, undergraduate advising, curriculum development, and assessment. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 months Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/02/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: No ABD consideration (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Applications must include (i) a cover letter that includes information on how the applicant’s research and teaching interests will complement and/or synergize with current departmental offerings (2 pages max), (ii) a curriculum vitae, (iii) a research statement that highlights short-term and long-term goals and the mentorship of undergraduate and master’s student researchers (3 pages max ), (iv) a teaching statement that includes philosophy, specific interests, and experience/training (2 pages max), and (v) the contact information for 3 references (name, address, telephone, email). UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 07/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 08/15/2026 Search Chair Name Darren Seals, Annkatrin Rose - co-chairs Search Chair Email sealsdf@appstate.edu, rosea@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54805 Posting Number FA00523P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56013": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Lecturer",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Lecturer Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Provide Rank Lecturer Position Number 0A1051 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Computer Information Systems - 255100 Working Location (City, State) Remote Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in a business-related field Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) A strong preference will be given to candidates with education in computer information systems or a related discipline, along with prior teaching experience in higher education and analytics with spreadsheet technology. It is also preferred that the successful candidate hold the MOS Excel Associate 365 Apps certification at the time of hire or commit to obtaining it within 60 days of employment (administered through the CIS department). Experience troubleshooting technical issues in computing environments is highly desirable. The position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to support students and faculty in technology-based learning and assessment settings. License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Computer Information Systems is housed in the Walker College of Business https://business.appstate.edu/ at Appalachian State University. The Walker College of Business is committed to ensuring that its graduates are equipped to succeed in an increasingly innovative, multicultural, and interdependent world. Details about department programs and faculty/staff can be found at https://cis.appstate.edu/ . Essential Duties and Responsibilities This is a remote position with primary responsibility for teaching the introductory spreadsheet analytics course ( CIS 1060) in the Flight Path program . Each course assignment is delivered over an 8-week term, with the teaching assignment distributed across the academic year as follows: ● Fall 1: 2 courses ● Fall 2: 2 courses ● Spring 1: 2 courses ● Spring 2: 2 courses ● Summer: 2 courses The Lecturer will be expected to effectively use and manage technology platforms that support online instruction and assessment, using Canvas as the learning management system, GMetrix for exam preparation and assessment, Microsoft Excel and Microsoft 365, and other instructional and testing platforms that support student learning and certification activities. The Lecturer will also be expected to participate in service activities at the program, department, college, university, profession, and community levels, and responsibilities will include coaching and mentoring students. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 11 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 01/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: N/A - ABD is not applicable for this position. See Minimum Qualifications. ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: Cover letter Resume or Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information for three references Evidence of successful teaching, such as teaching evaluations if prior classroom experience is indicated (attach under Evidence of Teaching) Statement of Teaching UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/16/2026 Search Chair Name Pranith Abbaraju Search Chair Email abbarajup@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55940 Posting Number FA00600P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Evidence of Teaching Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
