    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/52147": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Procurement Associate",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Procurement Associate Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Procurement Associate Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide a minimum of 3 references on the application. Applications will be reviewed by the Campus Dining supervisors based on employment needs. A Food Service supervisor will contact prospective candidates to provide more details on the temporary position. Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Procurement Associate Location Boone, NC Position Number N32320 Department Campus Dining - Procurement/Storeroom - 170340 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Must be able to drive a box truck. Must be able to lift 50 lbs., with or without reasonable accommodation, on a regular basis. License/Certification Required Must have a valid NC drivers license. Essential Job Functions Inventory management process and procedures Data entry and database management Accuracy and accountability with record-keeping Lifting up to 50 lbs. frequently with or without reasonable accommodation Monitoring of HACCP and implementation of FIFO best practices State purchasing and approval guidelines. Highly organized and detail-oriented Time management and ability to accomplish assigned tasks independently Positive attitude and willingness to help assigned units with any additional tasks. ServSafe and Forklift Training required (training and fees provided) Preferred Qualifications Forklift training (fees provided) and basic computer skills. Work Schedule/Hours Campus Dining is a Sunday – Saturday, 6:00 am – 11:00 pm operation. Employees are scheduled two days off each week based on business need. Days off may not be consecutive days off. Actual schedule times may vary. Employees may be required to work some flex hours to support the needs of the business and/or for special campus events. Schedules will be adjusted as needed to provide coverage in these cases. Number of Hours Per Week 30 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Moderate to heavy lifting, with or without reasonable accommodation. Working intermittently in extreme cold conditions is required. Hiring Range $15.00-$18.00, based on experience Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 09/19/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide a minimum of 3 references on the application. Applications will be reviewed by the Campus Dining supervisors based on employment needs. A Food Service supervisor will contact prospective candidates to provide more details on the temporary position. Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/52145 Posting Number 201501001P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
