    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55810": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Accounting Technician",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Accounting Technician Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Accounting Technician Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Office of Rural Promise plans to fill two positions for temporary Accounting Technicians for the Appalachian State University GEAR UP and EIR grants. Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Accounting Technician Location Boone, NC Position Number N50585/N50595/N50564 Department Office of Rural Promise - 240105 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Graduation from High School and one year of experience in accounting work; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required n/a Essential Job Functions Apply considerable knowledge of government accounting methods, program laws and regulations, procedures, and accounting practices needed to perform the work. Apply the knowledge in a variety of technology, financial systems and packages to create and maintain data. Develop formulas for moderately complex spreadsheets. Maintain ongoing communication with partners to include county financial officers with an understanding of school district policies and procedures. Quarterly site visits with county finance and administrative teams to monitor compliance and provide other training as needed. Understanding of the federal regulations governing GEAR UP and other federal grants including but not limited to EDGAR , Code of Federal Regulations (Uniform Guidance), program statutes, and program regulations. Attention to detail, organization, setting and meeting deadlines, and always remaining audit-ready are required. Effective collaboration skills are essential to working with the team, within administration, with the office of Special Funds Accounting, as well as with program coordinators on campus. Position requires effective analyzing, examining, tracking, inquiring, and ensuring deadlines are met for match and reimbursement packets, which are submitted on a monthly basis from 11 different counties across western North Carolina. Critical thinking skills are necessary to provide regular recommendations for improved efficiencies in processes and procedures. An operational mindset is required. Preferred Qualifications Prefer individual to have experience with travel procedures, purchasing procedures, Grants Management, and aspects of University funding. Bachelor’s degree in a related field from an accredited institution is preferred. Work Schedule/Hours Monday – Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position Normal office environment Hiring Range $20-$22 per hour Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/26/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants The Office of Rural Promise plans to fill two positions for temporary Accounting Technicians for the Appalachian State University GEAR UP and EIR grants. Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55807 Posting Number 201500569P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe in detail your experience using Microsoft Excel.  Specifically, what types of formulas or other features of excel have you used and for what purpose? (Open Ended Question) * What is your definition of excellent customer service? (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your communication skills (verbal and written) and how they will help you in performing the duties of this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
