    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55682": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Access Consultant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Access Consultant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application or attach a List of References with contact information included Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Access Consultant Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank Provide Rank Position Number 098371 Department Access & Opportunity: Disability Resources - 620000 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Office of Access & Opportunity is part of the Division of Institutional Integrity and provides leadership to the University’s efforts to foster a welcoming and accessible environment. The office promotes opportunity in educational opportunity, programming, and employment and promotes an environment of respect while honoring civil rights for all members of the University community. The Office of Access & Opportunity is comprised of Disability Resources and Equal Opportunity. The Disability Resources ( ODR ) unit of Access & Opportunity is the designated office at Appalachian State University for promoting opportunity, access, and civil rights based on a disability. ODR oversees access needs, applicable University resources/supports, and eligibility of appropriate accommodations (adjustments, auxiliary aids/services and reasonable modifications) based on disability for students and visitors. ODR is also responsible for oversight of accessibility of programs, services and activities; disability compliance requirements; and the facilitation of removing existing disability-related barriers within the built environment. Minimum Qualifications Two (2) years of progressive experience working directly with individuals with disabilities Demonstrated knowledge, training or experience interpreting federal and state laws regarding disability rights Demonstrated knowledge of determining eligibility for disability-related accommodations Bachelor’s degree in Clinical Psychology, Counselor Education, Special Education, Psychological or Rehabilitation Counseling, Social Work, Student Affairs or related discipline License/Certification Required Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a disability resource office at an institution of higher education Direct experience reviewing documentation and determining eligibility for disability-related accommodations Masters Degree in human services field such as Rehabilitation Counseling, Psychology, Social Work or related field Familiarity with various neuropsychological, psycho-educational and psychological assessment batteries used in the diagnosis of learning disabilities, Attention-Deficit/ Hyperactivity Disorder ( ADHD ) and traumatic brain injuries Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Access Consultant reports directly to the Associate Director of Disability Resources and is responsible for supporting the mission of the Office of Access and Opportunity: Disability Resources through: Coordination of the interactive process and evaluation of requests for and coordination of, accommodations, approved academic adjustments, workplace accommodations, auxiliary aids & services Review of student requests for accommodations and evaluating disability documentation, determining eligibility of academic adjustments, accommodations, and access needs Development of office guidelines and procedures Education and outreach for the Office of Access and Opportunity: Disability Resources ( ODR ) by coordinating outreach and initiatives for training with constituent groups and the campus community regarding disability-related topics Distribution of information to the university community related to the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ) and Section 504 Rehabilitation Act, disability issues, including, but not limited to being evaluated, the provision of reasonable accommodations, on-campus resources and off-campus agency support Consultation with faculty and staff regarding accessibility and the implementation of accommodations/academic adjustments Promotion of access to university programs and activities Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday - Friday with some flexible working hours and evenings Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $54,284 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/14/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 08/31/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 10/05/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application or attach a List of References with contact information included Search Chair Name Ellen Bunn Search Chair Email bunnek@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55680 Posting Number 201501829P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54234": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Support Services Associate",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Support Services Associate Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Support Services Associate Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Support Services Associate Location Boone, NC Position Number N37010/N37110/N37120 Department University Bookstore - Administration - 170500 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Graduation from high school or an equivalent combination of education and experience. License/Certification Required na Essential Job Functions The University Campus Store is a multi-faceted retail outlet right in the center of campus. See our website for a list of services we provide to our campus and public community. https://campusstore.appstate.edu/ University Campus Store Rental distribution and retrieval,including: Sales floor and textbook resets. Checking in new products/books and restocking the sales floor. Using a computer to fulfill & check accuracy of orders. Picking and packing book orders. Distribution of orders. General Merchandise Online Order Processing. Preferred Qualifications Good communication skills – Customer service skills – Ability to multi task – Basic windows based computer skills – Ability to pick up unfamiliar computer programs easily Work Schedule/Hours The position is based on the needs of each semester. Specific Dates vary but General times needed are as follows: Textbook Distribution – 2 – 4 weeks in January and August Textbook Retrieval – 2 – 3 weeks in May and December Textbook Reset &amp; Summer Distributions – 1-2 weeks possible in May, June and July General Merchandise – Occasional help needed for yearly inventory, Summer online order fulfillment and Fall Football season merchandise restocking and Game day help. Normal Hours of Operations: Monday – Thursday 8am – 6pm, Friday 8am – 5pm, Saturday 10am – 3pm, Closed Sundays As needed for up to 40 hours per week. Number of Hours Per Week up to 40 hours per week Number of Months Per Year 7 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $14.00-16.00 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 05/12/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference Special Instructions to Applicants Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54233 Posting Number 201501086P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you a current Appalachian State University Student? Yes No This position deals mostly with order fulfillment, do you have any experience in picking, verifying and/or packing orders to be sent to customers? 0 years 6 months-1 year 1-3 years 3-5 years 5+ years Please comment on your work experience with the following:\r\n\r\nHandling stress and pressure in the workplace. (Open Ended Question) Do you have customer service experience? Yes No Please describe your computer skills. (Open Ended Question) Please describe the experience you have with Point of Sale systems. (Open Ended Question) Do you have cash register experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55932": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Event Operations Supervisor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Event Operations Supervisor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application Reminder: if hired, employee must be willing to work nights and weekends Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title University Program Associate Working Title Event Operations Supervisor Location Boone NC Job Category 5 Position Number 093981 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Holmes Convocation Center - 170490 Primary Purpose of Position The central focus of the Event Operations Supervisor is to work closely with the Event Operations Manager, contributing to the determination, coordination, and supervision of the maintenance of production equipment within the center. This role involves the direct oversight and management of the APP ELITE Event Team, a dynamic assembly comprising up to 300 student and non-student temporary employees. The Event Operations Supervisor plays a pivotal role in the supervision of the Event Operations team, ensuring smooth event changeovers and efficient setup/tear downs. Core responsibilities encompass the recruitment and training of the APP ELITE Event Team staff, with a key emphasis on planning, scheduling, coordinating, and supervising their activities. Serving as a technical liaison between the staff and facility users, the Event Operations Supervisor is instrumental in ensuring effective communication and the successful execution of events. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; or equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all positions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Plan and execute diverse university program events, overseeing day-to-day functions and interpreting policies Deliver exceptional customer service, exhibiting excellent communication skills with clients, stakeholders, and internal teams Lead and supervise the APP ELITE Event Team, coordinating transactional services and addressing procedural issues Possess comprehensive knowledge of event logistics, audio/video/lighting equipment, and uphold safety compliance, preferred Recruit, train, and coordinate activities of the APP ELITE Event Team, overseeing program areas and administrative support Other duties deemed necessary or as directed Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position The Event Operations Supervisor in this position brings a wealth of knowledge and skills to oversee the seamless execution of events. With a comprehensive understanding of event planning, logistical coordination, budgeting, and risk management, they play a pivotal role in ensuring the success of various activities. Their technical proficiency extends to general audio, video, and lighting equipment, coupled with familiarity in event setups, staging, and general production equipment. Upholding safety compliance is paramount, with a keen awareness of state and federal OSHA requirements, ADA regulations, and NFPA codes and standards. Proficient in interpreting event layouts on CAD drawings, the Event Operations Supervisor possesses the organizational excellence needed to manage complex event logistics. In addition to their technical acumen: The supervisor excels in leadership, showcasing the ability to coach, mentor, and motivate a diverse team. Operating with independence, they exhibit good judgment and initiative in handling responsibilities. Strong troubleshooting skills enable them to address issues promptly and safely during events, while excellent communication skills facilitate effective interaction with clients, stakeholders, and internal teams. The ability to plan, coordinate, and supervise changeover/conversion crews efficiently underscores their role. Dependability is a hallmark, demonstrated through punctuality, adherence to varying shifts, and timely completion of responsibilities. Adept at multitasking and stress management, the Event Operations Supervisor builds and maintains robust client relationships, embodying a commitment to understanding and exceeding client expectations. Overall, this position requires a versatile and skilled professional capable of orchestrating diverse events with precision and expertise. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Previous work in the event management and/or hospitality industry Previous experience in supervising teams of staff Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Leading Work Teams : Take charge as the leader of the campus-wide APP ELITE Event Team, spearheading an efficient and effective event staff. Conduct thorough training sessions for students, equipping them with the necessary skills for the proper use of all equipment. Provide comprehensive training for various front-of-house positions such as ushers, security personnel, and ticket takers, as well as for roles involving loading, event setup, and other responsibilities. Maintain a vigilant presence, continuously monitoring the work of student employees to ensure the correct setup of stages, steps, seats, tables, and other event elements. Conduct comprehensive safety checks by walking through all areas in use before events, identifying and mitigating potential hazards, ensuring a secure environment. As a proactive leader, prioritize safety by ensuring that all production crews utilizing the facility adhere to safe practices. Conduct thorough inspections, including rigging and cable runs, to guarantee their safety and functionality before opening doors for an event. This role emphasizes a commitment to a secure and well-executed event environment, placing emphasis on leadership, training, and meticulous safety measures. Program Administration: The role involves comprehensive oversight of the APP ELITE Event Team, encompassing the meticulous scheduling and planning of both daily tasks and event-related projects. Effective management of event staffing schedules is a priority, ensuring optimal coverage and seamless coordination. Direct supervision of event conversions and set-ups is undertaken with a commitment to efficient execution. Proactive engagement with promoters, managers, and stakeholders is essential, involving the gathering of necessary information and advancing event details. Collaborative efforts with promoters and managers are integral to ensuring timely request fulfillment, emphasizing a client-oriented service approach. Regular reviews of existing procedures and recommendations for new or revised processes are conducted, providing valuable insights for continuous improvement. Additionally, responsibility is assumed for the maintenance and storage of specialized technical production equipment to ensure operational readiness and longevity. In this role, coordination of students, temps, and contractors is pivotal, focusing on timely, efficient, and safe conversions from one event to the next. Primarily working overnight with limited supervision, this position holds a high degree of responsibility to ensure thorough event setups. Collaboration with outside vendors, laborers, and services becomes necessary, especially during periods when students are out of school. Identifying equipment and product needs, researching manufacturers and suppliers, and procuring necessary items for events or programs are integral responsibilities. The position also may involve proposing innovative approaches to enhance the efficiency and safety of event conversions. Knowledge-Program & Organization: Familiarity with and adherence to State, University, and Holmes Center policies is essential. Possess comprehensive knowledge of sound and lighting equipment, encompassing their uses and designs. Demonstrate expertise in event operations, covering both front-of-house and back-of-house processes. Maintain a foundational understanding of basic rigging principles. Ensure the functionality of all technical equipment by conducting regular checks and promptly addressing any issues to uphold proper and safe use. Undertake routine maintenance on equipment to guarantee ongoing functionality and safety compliance. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Regular hours are from 9:00am-5:00pm Monday-Friday, but nights and weekends (and sometimes long shifts) are required based on event schedule and as approved by the Supervisor. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Overall Competency Level Journey Salary Grade Equivalency GN07 Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $42,436 - $44,218 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date 09/27/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application Reminder: if hired, employee must be willing to work nights and weekends Search Chair Name Trevor Rowe Search Chair Email roweta1@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55852 Posting Number 201503038P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have experience in Event Operations? Yes No If you do have experience in Event Operations, please explain: (Open Ended Question) Please describe any experience you have working with preparations for special events and/or meetings. (Open Ended Question) Please comment on your work experience with the following:\r\n\r\nSupervising student workers. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/46011": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Part Time Special Faculty of Supply Chain Management - Boone Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Part Time Special Faculty of Supply Chain Management - Boone Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter ● CV ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Part Time Special Faculty of Supply Chain Management - Boone Department Marketing & Supply Chain Mgmt (SCM) - 255350 Location Boone, NC Position Number 006818 Description of Department Marketing & Supply Chain Management is currently the largest department (in terms of undergraduate degree seeking students) of six departments within the John A. Walker College of Business. Business students may choose from three marketing concentrations – General Marketing, Digital Marketing or Professional Selling. The department also offers minors in professional selling (for business majors), sales (for non-business majors) and general marketing (for non-business majors). Additionally, business students can earn a Supply Chain Management major or minor. Graduate level courses are offered in the MBA / MS in Analytics program. Location of this position is Boone Campus. The Marketing & Supply Chain Management Department consists of 16 tenured/ tenure track and 11 adjunct faculty members. The Walker College of Business is one of the largest public business schools for undergraduate students in the University of North Carolina system. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Business, Supply Chain Management, or closely related field. Essential Job Functions The person who fills this position will be expected to provide instruction primarily in Principles of Supply Chain Management, Global Supply Chain and Logistics, Strategic Procurement and Global Sourcing, and Operations Management. Instructional duties will include a teaching load of up to six credit hours per semester and participation in curriculum development. In addition to instructional duties, faculty members will be expected to contribute to service activities such as alumni relations, participation in student recruiting activities, and other departmental activities. Preferred Qualifications The department is especially interested in candidates with teaching interests in one or more of the following areas – Supply Chain Management, Operations Management, Logistics, and/or Procurement. Number of Hours Per Week TBD - Part Time, Semester to Semester Number of Months per Year 9 Hiring Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Posting Details Posting Date 05/13/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire Evaluation of Applications Begins 05/13/2024 Search Chair Name Stephanie J. Lawson Search Chair Email lawsonsj1@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter ● CV ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55020": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Director of Partnerships &amp; Engagement",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Director of Partnerships &amp; Engagement Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Director of Partnerships & Engagement Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach required documents: Cover Letter addressing the candidates alignment with the responsibilities of the job Resume List of 3 Professional References with Contact Information Included Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Director of Partnerships & Engagement Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank Position Number 044501 Department College of Education - 260000 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Director of Partnerships and Engagement is responsible for developing, managing, and sustaining strong partnerships between the Reich College of Education and external stakeholders, public schools, and others. The Director oversees the strategic direction of the College’s collaborative efforts with external partners, public schools and others, and plays a crucial role in aligning the College’s strategic priorities with the needs of external partners. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in education or a closely related field Hold or be eligible for a North Carolina Teaching or Administrative License Teaching and leadership experience within PK–12 educational settings Demonstrated ability to cultivate and sustain collaborative partnerships between higher education and public school systems and others Strong organizational, written, and verbal communication skills Effective interpersonal and team leadership skills with the ability to work seamlessly across both university and public school and other external environments Proficiency in using technology to support communication and collaboration among stakeholders License/Certification Required Hold or be eligible for a NC Teaching or Administrator License Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in education or a closely related field National Board Certification Familiarity with higher education systems, particularly in the context of educator preparation programs Demonstrated experience in writing and securing grants Strong understanding of state-level education policies and legislation, with the ability to effectively articulate to others Experience in designing and delivering professional development for educators Proven ability to plan, coordinate, and execute events Proficiency in educational technology tools, social media management, and website maintenance Experience supervising staff or leading teams Essential Duties and Responsibilities Strategic Planning and Leadership Develop and implement a comprehensive strategic plan for the Public School and other external Partnership. Align the goals with the College’s mission and strategic priorities. Lead initiatives that strengthen partnerships between the College and external partners. Coordinate and plan with the Public School Partnership Advisory Board. Coordinate and plan meetings and initiatives with other external partners. Serve as the Regional Director of the North Carolina New Teacher Support Program ( NCNTSP ). Supervise the NCNTSP coaches. Partnership Development, Management, and Sustainability Serve as the primary liaison between the College and public schools and other external partners, ensuring effective communication and collaboration. Collaborate with district leaders, school administrators, teachers, and university faculty to identify opportunities for partnership initiatives, including joint projects, research, and professional development. Support public school and other external partners by providing professional development, resources, and special programming. Monitor and be informed about P-12 education policy as it affects public schools. Collaborate with university faculty and staff and public school partners to strengthen the educator pipeline. Manage the day-to-day operations of the Office of Partnerships & Engagement, including budgeting, staffing, and resource allocation. Monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of partnership and engagement initiatives, making adjustments as necessary. Prepare reports, presentations, and other documentation to communicate the impact of partnership initiatives to internal and external audiences. Identify and pursue funding opportunities to support partnership and engagement initiatives. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday - Friday 8:00-5:00 Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range Commensurate with experience Physical Demands of Position This position requires regular travel to public schools and other external partnerships across the northwest region, the university’s lab school, and local, state, and national meetings, conferences, and events. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/02/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 07/20/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 09/07/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach required documents: Cover Letter addressing the candidates alignment with the responsibilities of the job Resume List of 3 Professional References with Contact Information Included Search Chair Name Monica Lambert Search Chair Email lambertma@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54960 Posting Number 201501805P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
