    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55699": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Practitioner in Residence for the Department of Management (Hickory Campus) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Practitioner in Residence for the Department of Management (Hickory Campus) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Practitioner in Residence for the Department of Management (Hickory Campus) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Provide Rank Practitioner in Residence Position Number 097401 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Management - 255300 Working Location (City, State) Hickory, North Carolina Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications A Master’s Degree in Business or a closely related discipline is required. If the Master’s degree is in an area other than business, candidates must have received at least 18 credit hours in the discipline in which they would teach. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) The department seeks qualified candidates with relevant industry experience. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in Ethical and Sustainable Management, Evidence-Based Management, Organizational Behavior, and Human Resource Management. We are especially interested in individuals who demonstrate a strong commitment to student coaching and mentorship. Given the needs of our growing campus in Hickory, N.C., a strong commitment to community engagement and business outreach is essential. Additionally, teaching experience at the college level and 10+ years of relevant industry experience is preferred. License/Certification Required Description of the Department or Unit In the Department of Management , we are a vibrant community of teachers, scholars, and professional practitioners that are passionate about developing the next generation of business leaders. Our faculty have studied at the best universities in the world, have led global enterprises, and are successful entrepreneurs. The department offers two undergraduate Bachelor of Science in Business Administration ( BSBA ) degree programs: the major in management ( MGT ) and the major in hospitality and tourism management ( HOS ). The department also offers, for both business and non-business majors, minors in innovation & entrepreneurship, human resource management, and sustainable business. At the graduate level, the Industrial-Organizational Psychology and Human Resource Management Program ( IOHRM ) is an interdisciplinary and award-winning Master of Arts degree program offered jointly by the Department of Management and Department of Psychology. Also, management faculty provide instruction in the Master of Business Administration ( MBA ) program offered by the Walker College of Business. The Walker College is an AACSB -accredited business school, and in 2019 was featured in The Princeton Review’s edition of Best Business Schools. The Department of Management is the largest department within the Walker College of Business, which itself has the largest business school enrollment in the 17-campus UNC system (approximately 3,000 students). Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Management Department at Appalachian State University invites applications for a non-tenure track, nine-month Practitioner-in-Residence faculty position beginning January 2027. The position will primarily serve Appalachian State’s satellite campus in Hickory, NC. The faculty will teach four (4) management classes per semester and is encouraged to engage and develop relationships with the business community. Primary teaching duties will be in-person courses and holding office hours on the Hickory campus. Teaching duties may also include online and/or hybrid courses. The department seeks qualified candidates with relevant industry experience. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in Ethical and Sustainable Management, Evidence-Based Management, Organizational Behavior, and Human Resource Management. We are especially interested in individuals who demonstrate a strong commitment to student coaching and mentorship. Given the needs of our growing campus, a strong commitment to engaging with local businesses and community partners is essential. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 01/04/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: N/A - ABD is not applicable for this position. See Minimum Qualifications. ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Curriculum Vita Unofficial Graduate Transcripts (Academic Affairs requests these be included in external searches) List of three professional references with contact information included UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 08/18/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 08/26/2026 Search Chair Name Melissa Carsten Search Chair Email carstenmk@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55579 Posting Number FA00575P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s Degree in Business; or if you have a Master's Degree in a closely related discipline, do you have at least 18 credit hours in the discipline in which you would teach? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Teaching Evaluations & Peer Reviews Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54280": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant or Associate Professor Position Number 008651 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Child Development, Literacy, and Special Education - 260200 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in special education or closely related field by August 2027 – Candidates who are ABD will be considered, but the position requires successful completion of all doctoral requirements by the start date Minimum of three years of teaching or clinical experience with students with disabilities Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) We are looking for candidates who bring expertise in at least TWO of the following areas (in terms of teaching and/or research). Please explicitly identify and discuss at least TWO areas in your letter of interest: Online undergraduate and/or graduate teaching experience and course development Supervising teacher candidates in clinical or field-based settings Knowledge of multi-tiered systems of support and evidence-based practices in academic instruction, with experience teaching a range of disabilities Candidates with an established record of, or potential for, securing external funding Knowledge of administration, law, and policy Candidates should demonstrate evidence of, or potential for, university teaching and scholarship related to students with disabilities License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Special Education Program within the Reich College of Education at Appalachian State University is one of the largest in North Carolina with nine full-time special education faculty who offer in person and online BS and MA degrees in special education, an undergraduate minor in special education, and graduate certificates in autism, special education leadership, and emotional/behavioral disorders. The program prepares educators to teach students with a range of disabilities as well as an ability to analyze how social justice intersects with our schools, especially as they are manifested on local, state, and national levels. The Reich College of Education also offers a doctorate in Educational Leadership, including a concentration in Literacy and Exceptionalities, providing faculty with opportunities to chair or serve on doctoral committees. Appalachian State University is a member of the sixteen-campus University of North Carolina. Located in Boone, North Carolina, the University enrolls over 20,000 students, primarily in Bachelors and Masters programs. Appalachian has a traditional residential campus and a variety of distance education programs. Additional information about the Department of Child Development, Literacy, and Special Education, the university, and the surrounding area is located at https://clse.appstate.edu . The campus is located in the Blue Ridge Mountains of Western North Carolina, a region noted for its scenic beauty. We are near the Appalachian Trail, the Blue Ridge Parkway, and national and state parks. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Department of Child Development, Literacy, and Special Education in the Reich College of Education at Appalachian State University seeks qualified candidates to fill one tenure-track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in Special Education. We are seeking applicants with expertise in teaching and an active research agenda in special education to join our collaborative team. The successful applicant will be appointed to a full-time, nine-month position beginning in August 2027, with the possibility of summer teaching. The duties include teaching, research, and service. Specific responsibilities will include: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses both in person and online Conduct engaging scholarly work Provide service to the program, department, college, university, profession, and community Collaborate with colleagues in the program, department, university, and Pre-K-12 schools Advise graduate students Serve on doctoral committees Demonstrate commitment to the university’s strategic plan and/or department mission/goals Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/09/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. APPLICATION PROCEDURE AND TIMELINE : For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: A letter of application that includes a description addressing the listed required minimum qualiﬁcations , essential duties and responsibilities, and identification of at least two areas of interest listed in this job description ; Current vita ; and Contact information for three references familiar with the candidate who can speak to the candidate’s teaching and scholarship qualifications. Unofficial Transcripts (Graduate and Doctoral) – no password-protected files For additional information and inquiries, contact Dan Poling (828) 262-6075/polingdv@appstate.edu) and Debra Prykanowski (828) 262-8388/prykanowskida@appstate.edu). Review of complete applications will begin October 1, 2026, and we will continue to accept and review applications until the position is filled. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 05/14/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Dan Poling and Debra Prykanowski Search Chair Email polingdv@appstate.edu , prykanowskida@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54054 Posting Number FA00580P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55941": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Executive Assistant to the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Executive Assistant to the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Executive Assistant to the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please upload the below documents: Cover Letter Resume Please include 3 references with contact information in the body of the application Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Executive Assistant Working Title Executive Assistant to the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation Location Boone NC Job Category 5 Position Number 0A0131 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Office of Research and Innovation- 282000 Primary Purpose of Position The Office of Research and Innovation ( ORI ) supports Appalachian State University research, scholarship and creative activities ( RSCA ) with expertise in competitiveness, compliance, and innovative impacts. The ORI builds capacity and fosters success for App State researchers throughout the RSCA life-cycle, from ideation to real-world implications. Led by the Vice Chancellor for Research and Innovation, and consists of five divisions: Grants Resources & Services ( GRS ); Sponsored Programs (SP); Research Design & Analysis ( RDA ), Research Protections (RP), and Innovation in Practice (IP). ORI provides support for the research, creative, and scholarly endeavors of Appalachian faculty, staff, and students. ORI manages both internal and external funding programs and promotes business and industry partnerships. The primary purpose of this position is to provide high-level administrative support to the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation ( VCRI ) and the Office of Research and Innovation ( ORI ) at Appalachian State University. This role is responsible for managing day-to-day operations for the VCRI and facilitating the efficient functioning of the Research and Innovation division. The position serves as the first point of contact for the office, managing communications, calendars, and travel arrangements for the VCRI and providing limited support to the division and the ORI in the functional areas listed below. Job functions to support the purpose of this role will include activities such as these listed below, and may evolve based on the needs of the VCRI to support the research, scholarship and creative activity enterprise. Minimum Qualifications Graduation from high school and three years of progressively responsible administrative/office management experience; or graduation of a two-year secretarial science or business administration program and one year of experience as described above; or graduation from a four-year college or university, preferably with major emphasis on Business administration or a related field; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all positions. Degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions The Office of Research and Innovation ( ORI ) supports Appalachian State University research, scholarship and creative activities ( RSCA ) with expertise in competitiveness, compliance, and innovative impacts. The ORI builds capacity and fosters success for App State researchers throughout the RSCA life-cycle, from ideation to real-world implications. Led by the Vice Chancellor for Research and Innovation, and consists of five divisions: Grants Resources & Services ( GRS ); Sponsored Programs (SP); Research Design & Analysis ( RDA ), Research Protections (RP), and Innovation in Practice (IP). ORI provides support for the research, creative, and scholarly endeavors of Appalachian faculty, staff, and students. ORI manages both internal and external funding programs and promotes business and industry partnerships. The primary purpose of this position is to provide high-level administrative support to the Vice Chancellor for Research and Innovation ( VCRI ) and the Office of Research and Innovation ( ORI ) at Appalachian State University. This role is responsible for managing day-to-day operations for the VCRI and facilitating the efficient functioning of the ORI . The position serves as the first point of contact for the office, managing communications, calendars, and travel arrangements for the VCRI and providing limited support to the ORI team. Job functions to support the purpose of this role will include activities such as these listed below, and may evolve based on the needs of the VCRI to support the research, scholarship and creative activity enterprise: 1. VCRI Executive Support Manage VCRI’s calendar Handle communications, including email triage and drafting Coordinate all aspects of travel Draft letters and correspondence Make room reservations Maintain NSF documents for VCRI 2. ORI Team Support Assist with large group calendaring for big meetings Provide limited travel support (e.g., blanket authorizations, conference registrations) 3. Office Management Manage purchasing/procurement for ORI office supplies, inventory, and promotional items Serve as the first point of contact for ORI , handling email and physical mail/shipping Coordinate employee onboarding (keys, mailbox, furniture, phone line, laptop/equipment, signage) Serve as a member of the Building Emergency Team ( BET ) Manage building repairs/work orders for JET building and space management 4. Administrative Tasks Manage internal committee memberships and appointments Work with ORI Business Officer to organize records/documents physically and digitally Serve as Business Officer backup and payroll originator proxy Take meeting notes/minutes (IP Council, URC , etc.) Maintain Google Drive folder structure and organization 5. Executive Support Prevent scheduling conflicts and resolve competing priorities Independently assimilate and compose materials for the VCRI Establish and maintain paper and electronic files and records for the VCRI Assist VPR with personnel administration (job searches, AppState Careers) 6. Events and Communications Plan and manage logistics for ORI events and activities Provide scheduling and administrative support for campus-wide events Serve as point of contact for URC and IP, managing all correspondence Manage correspondence with the Chancellor’s and Provost’s Offices for research-related matters Edit documents to incorporate VCRI’s personal style Serve as UComms Liaison for ORI Collaborate with UComm ORI experts to manage the Office of Research and Innovation website and social media Support light graphic design needs Provide administrative support for research Google group posts, Workshop Scheduler, and Research News Capture and share stories for submittal to ORI UComm team member 7. General Support Assist with Workshop Scheduler Update Research News on ORI homepage Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required: This position requires organizational and communication skills, including the ability to manage complex calendars, prioritize tasks, and draft professional correspondence. Proficiency in various software applications and adaptability to new technologies is needed. Attention to detail, multitasking capabilities in a fast-paced environment, and sound judgment in decision-making are expected. Familiarity with university policies and procedures, particularly in research administration and personnel management, is necessary. Interpersonal skills for interaction with broad stakeholders, discretion in handling confidential information, and flexibility in addressing changing priorities are required. A problem-solving approach and customer-service orientation support the VCRI and the Research and Innovation division, including the Office of Research and Innovation, in achieving their strategic goals. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and one year of experience related to the area of assignment; or equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Communication & Marketing: Must maintain critical communications at high levels of the organization and requires the ability to convey potentially sensitive information. Collaborate with UComm ORI expert to manage Office of Research and Innovation website and social media and must have the ability to plan and implement marketing strategies and functions. Adaption of communication styles and drafting high-level correspondence for the VCRI . Must have the ability to communicate complex information effectively with a range of audiences, including senior leadership. Serve as UComm Liaison for ORI with advanced interpersonal skills to build and maintain professional relationships across organizational lines. We require an individual with the ability to facilitate communication between different departments and adapt messaging for various audiences. Leadership: Plan and manage logistics for ORI events, programs, plans and activities. Provide consultation on issues and requests from clients (in this case, those involved in the events). Manage, organize and coordinate internal committee memberships and appointments. Ability to develop and implement short-term strategies consistent with program goals. Information Analysis/Decision Making: Work with ORI Business Officer to organize records/documents physically and digitally. We require an individual with the ability to gather, organize, and analyze program information and data. They will be involved in making decisions about how to best organize and manage this information. Independently assimilate and compose materials for the VCRI through the analysis of information and make decisions about what to include in materials for the VCRI . Assess and resolve potentially unprecedented problems that require research and review of policies and procedures. Consultancy Skills: Prevent scheduling conflicts and resolve competing priorities through advice and collaboration with the VCRI and other stakeholders to resolve difficult issues. It involves applying knowledge of program culture and work relationships to address situations. Serve as UComms Liaison for ORI and identify trends, recognize the impact of policies and procedures, and promote best practices in communication. It involves collaborating with various stakeholders to achieve mutually agreeable outcomes. Program/Project Administration: Manage VCRI’s calendar and coordinate all aspects of travel for the efficient operation of the VCRI’s office and the broader ORI program. Must have the ability to define scope, goals, tasks, deliverables, and timelines through the development and monitoring of schedules and ensuring program accountability. Administer a component of the broader ORI program through the management of purchasing/procurement for ORI office supplies, inventory, and promotional items. Must have the ability to assess the needs of the work unit, determine any gaps, make technical decisions about procurement and ensure program accountability of resources. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Typically Mon-Fri, 8:00 – 5:00 in office, some weekend and evening work as needed and approved by supervisor. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position General office environment. Some light lifting may be required from time to time. All duties are to be performed with or without reasonable accommodation. Overall Competency Level Advanced Salary Grade Equivalency GN11 Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $64,373 - $72,100 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date 09/13/2026 Competency Level Statement If no applicants apply who meet the required competencies, then management may consider other applicants at a lower competency level. Special Instructions to Applicants To be considered, please upload the below documents: Cover Letter Resume Please include 3 references with contact information in the body of the application Search Chair Name Christine Hendren Search Chair Email hendrenco@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55843 Posting Number 201503037P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55861": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Food Service Supervisor - Crossroads Café Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Food Service Supervisor - Crossroads Café Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For consideration, please attach the following: Resume and/or CV Cover Letter is Optional on the documents page Include at least 3 references in the body of the application Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Food Services Supervisor-ASU Working Title Food Service Supervisor - Crossroads Café Location Boone, NC Job Category 8 Position Number 038461 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Campus Dining - Crossroads Coffee House - 170530 Primary Purpose of Position To be an effective supervisor for Appalachian State University Campus Dining by managing work processes and performance. Present a positive and professional image at all times. To serve the Appalachian community using sustainable practices, creative and intentional menus, and engaging customer service. Assisting assigned unit with any additional assigned tasks after completing primary duties. Minimum Qualifications Graduation from High School or possession of a GED , and one year of experience in food preparation or service activities in a commercial kitchen; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Experience in the field of work related to the position’s role may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Supervises all full-time, temporary and student employees in assigned area. Orders food supplies and completes work orders for equipment repair. Recognizes potential problems in service, addresses, and resolves promptly and respectfully. Facilitates communication among the work groups in a manner that helps accomplish daily work goals. All ASU Campus Dining employees are required to work during home football games or any other special campus event as needed. Campus work location may vary depending on the event. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Knowledge of personnel management and food production. Good time management and food safety skills. Ability to delegate tasks to student and full-time employees. Ability to ensure good customer service by helping train and coach all employees in their charge. Ability to plan and coordinate breaks and schedules to ensure proper coverage of meal service. Manage daily unit operations. Must possesses the skills to do maintenance on all our coffee shop machines and equipment across all campus dining units. The ability to program espresso, grinders and coffee makers across all campus dining units. Preferred Qualifications 2 years of related Barista and coffee shop maintenance experience; Preferred Coffee Machine Maintenance certification Preferred Coffee Shop or QSR supervision Obtain ServSafe for Management certification within 1 year of employment Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Communication, Customer Service, Interpersonal Skills, Knowledge-Technical, Safety and Health Compliance Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Campus Dining is a Sunday – Saturday, 6:00 am – 11:00 pm operation. Operations are reduced during university breaks. Employees are scheduled two days off each week based on business need. Days off may not be consecutive days off. Employees may be required to work some flex hours to support the needs of the business and/or for special campus events. Schedules will be adjusted as needed to provide coverage in these cases. Employees are considered mandatory staff and are subject to call back anytime 365 days a year. Report to work on alternating holidays to check all food service buildings. When required employee must make needed repairs during holiday and weekend checks. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Requires a significant amount of time on your feet as much as the full 8 hours you are here. Must be able to deal with extreme heat and cold at times in a fast-paced environment. Must be able to lift and move heavy equipment weighing up to 100 lbs. on a daily basis without any restrictions. This position must be able to remain stationary 50% of the time. This position needs the ability to traverse a crowded area multiple times a day. Work in this position requires the sustained use of a computer and other office equipment. This position requires the ability to communicate ideas and needs as well as understanding and answering questions and concerns from staff. This position requires the ability to observe details at a close range. Overall Competency Level Journey Salary Grade Equivalency 50 Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $42,177 - $44,200 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/30/2026 Closing Date 09/13/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants For consideration, please attach the following: Resume and/or CV Cover Letter is Optional on the documents page Include at least 3 references in the body of the application Search Chair Name Anna Loggins Search Chair Email logginsan@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55466 Posting Number 201503022P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have knowledge of standard sanitation practices necessary to ensure safe handling of food? Yes No Do you have a basic knowledge of food service equipment? Yes No Do you have food service experience in a high volume location? Yes No Do you have experience supervising other employees (both student employees and full-time employees)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
