    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55087": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Regional Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Regional Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Regional Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a resume, cover letter/letter of interest, and a list of three professional references with contact information through the university's job board. Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Regional Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank N/A Position Number 0A0981 Department Office of Rural Promise - 240105 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator coordinates postsecondary academic and workforce pathways in Region 3, including community college transitions, university pathways, apprenticeships, scholar and fellow programs, certificate pathways, training-site connections, and employer placement. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in higher education, student services, workforce development, public health, health sciences, social work, counseling, business, education, or a related field. At least two years of experience in postsecondary advising, workforce development, employer engagement, career services, community college partnerships, transfer support, student services, or related work. Strong communication, coordination, documentation, and relationship management skills. Ability to travel across Region 3 (Alexander, Anson, Cabarrus, Catawba, Cleveland, Gaston, Iredell, Lincoln, Mecklenburg, Rowan, Stanly, and Union Counties). License/Certification Required No license or certification is required. Project management, workforce development, public health, clinical, or related certifications may be preferred where applicable. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Experience with community college transfer, health professions education, apprenticeships, work-based learning, NCWorks, Career Centers, rural workforce placement, or employer partnerships. Knowledge of Region 3 postsecondary institutions and employer networks. Experience tracking student progression, placements, or workforce outcomes. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator leads the coordination and advancement of postsecondary education-to-workforce pathways across Region 3 to strengthen regional health workforce development. This position develops and aligns community college transfer pathways, university partnerships, apprenticeships, certificates, scholar and fellow experiences, work-based learning opportunities, and employer connections to support learner progression into high-demand health careers and rural employment. The role serves as a regional connector among education, workforce, and employer partners to improve pathway access, placement, and retention outcomes. POSTSECONDARY PATHWAY DEVELOPMENT & COORDINATION Lead the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of coordinated postsecondary health workforce pathways across Region 3 (Alexander, Anson, Cabarrus, Catawba, Cleveland, Gaston, Iredell, Lincoln, Mecklenburg, Rowan, Stanly, and Union Counties). Facilitate alignment among community colleges, Appalachian State academic programs, four-year institutions, apprenticeship programs, certificate programs, and workforce partners to strengthen learner progression and reduce barriers to transition. Support pathway mapping, articulation, transfer planning, and cross-sector alignment to expand access to health professions education and employment opportunities. Coordinate regional strategies that connect educational experiences to workforce outcomes and support sustainable talent pipelines. STUDENT TRANSITION , NAVIGATION , & PLACEMENT Support student and trainee navigation across postsecondary education, work-based learning, and employment pathways. Coordinate opportunities including scholar and fellow programs, apprenticeships, clinical or experiential learning, paid work-based learning, certificate pathways, and early-career placement initiatives. Identify and expand training-site and placement capacity through collaboration with educational and employer partners. Develop strategies to strengthen learner persistence, transition success, rural placement, and workforce retention. PARTNERSHIP DEVELOPMENT & EMPLOYER ENGAGEMENT Build and maintain collaborative relationships with community colleges, university partners, NCWorks and Career Centers, employers, training sites, Vaya partners, faculty, advisors, and regional stakeholders. Facilitate regional engagement activities to identify workforce needs and align educational pathways with labor market demand. Represent Appalachian State in regional workforce and pathway initiatives and support implementation of collaborative regional strategies. DATA , REPORTING & CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT Track and monitor pathway participation, transfer activity, training-site utilization, placement outcomes, and workforce retention indicators. Support collection, analysis, and reporting of grant and program performance measures. Develop recommendations for process improvements and pathway enhancement based on regional data and stakeholder feedback. Support documentation, compliance requirements, and regional implementation workgroups. CROSS - SECTOR ALIGNMENT & REGIONAL IMPLEMENTATION Coordinate with the K–12 and Youth Pathways Coordinator to ensure seamless transition from youth engagement activities into postsecondary opportunities. Contribute to regional planning, implementation, and sustainability efforts to strengthen long-term health workforce outcomes. Support strategic initiatives of the Office of Rural Promise and regional grant objectives. OTHER Other duties as assigned. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; with some nights and weekends as needed for student programming. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $55,000-$60,000 Physical Demands of Position This position primarily involves office and computer-based work, including prolonged periods of sitting, typing, reading, virtual meetings, document review, and project communication. The position may require occasional travel to partner sites, schools, community colleges, healthcare organizations, meetings, and regional convenings. Occasional lifting or transport of meeting materials and supplies up to 20 pounds may be required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/13/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 07/27/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 08/03/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit a resume, cover letter/letter of interest, and a list of three professional references with contact information through the university’s job board. Search Chair Name Katie Matthews Search Chair Email matthewsk@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55086 Posting Number 201501810P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56026": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Director of Contracts and Grants Administration",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Director of Contracts and Grants Administration Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Director of Contracts and Grants Administration Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List of References with Contact Information Finalists will be subject to a criminal background check prior to the offer of employment. All candidate names and information will remain confidential; however, finalists invited to campus may be asked to waive confidentiality to engage with the broader campus community. References will not be contacted without a candidate’s prior knowledge and consent. Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Director of Contracts and Grants Administration Location Boone NC Faculty Rank Provide Rank Position Number 099911 Department Contracts and Grants Accounting - 415102 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose Division of Research and Innovation The Division of Research and Innovation ( DRI ) supports and advances Appalachian State University’s research, scholarship, creative activities, innovation, and public service mission by providing leadership, infrastructure, compliance oversight, strategic investment, and administrative support for the university’s research enterprise. The division encompasses the Office of Research and Innovation ( ORI ), which includes research administration, sponsored programs, contracts and grants accounting, compliance functions, internal funding programs, and innovation and commercialization initiatives. Beyond the ORI , the DRI includes other strategic research and creative activity operations that support faculty, staff, and student success. The ORI supports and enhances the research, scholarship, creative activities, and public service initiatives by managing internal and external funding programs, providing research administration services, and supporting both funded and unfunded scholarly initiatives across the campus community. Click here to learn more about the other Office of Research and Innovation Departments About this role: The Director of Contracts and Grants Administration position reports to the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation and provides strategic and operational leadership for award set-up and post-award administration within the Office of Research and Innovation. This position ensures that faculty, staff, and institutional partners receive high-quality support from award through execution and closeout, while maintaining strong compliance, financial stewardship, and service-oriented practices. The Director supervises multiple Associate Directors and provides leadership for a team of approximately 12-15 staff members. In this role, the CGA Director will provide leadership, direction, and accountability for administration and accounting functions across the award acceptance and post-award lifecycle of grants and contracts, including post-award financial support, reporting, and closeout. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in business administration, public administration, accounting, finance, higher education administration, research administration, or a related field. Minimum of 8 years of progressively responsible experience in sponsored programs administration, research administration, grants management, contract and grant accounting, or a closely related field. Minimum of 5 years of supervisory or management experience leading professional staff and complex administrative operations. Demonstrated knowledge of federal sponsored project regulations, Uniform Guidance, sponsor requirements, and research administration best practices. Experience managing pre-award and post-award functions, including proposal submission, award administration, compliance, and financial oversight. Demonstrated ability to interpret regulations, exercise independent judgment, and communicate effectively with diverse stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to lead with a compass toward serving faculty and researcher needs while balancing with critical, reliable compliance requirements. License/Certification Required Preferred Qualifications A certified research administrator ( CRA ) credential is preferred. More than 10 years of progressively responsible experience in research administration or sponsored programs leadership. Experience leading both sponsored programs, contracting and grant accounting functions within a university or research-intensive environment. Experience supervising managers or directors and leading large, multi-functional teams. Professional certification such as Certified Research Administrator ( CRA ), Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator ( CPRA ), or Certified Financial Research Administrator ( CFRA ). Essential Duties and Responsibilities Leadership and Strategic Administration Provide leadership and oversight for all post-award administration and accounting functions across the Office of Research and Innovation. Manage the daily operations of the CGA department, ensuring effective coordination across pre- and post-award functions, contract negotiation, closeout, and reporting. Serve as a key advisor to the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation for research administration operations, financial compliance, staffing, systems, and strategic initiatives. Develop and implement strategic plans, operational priorities, and performance measures that advance institutional research and innovation goals. Lead organizational change initiatives, process improvements, and technology implementations that improve efficiency, transparency, and service delivery. Establish clear expectations, workflows, service standards, and performance measures that support timely, accurate, compliant, and customer-oriented service to faculty and campus partners. Collaboration with Pre-Award Administration Collaborate with the Director of Sponsored Programs on processes to ensure the effective integration of pre-award processes with the post-award compliance needs to execute the resulting agreements, including processes such as the review, preparation, negotiation, and execution of incoming and outgoing contracts, subawards, and research-related agreements. Share responsibility with the Vice Chancellor of Research and Innovation for ensuring that all sponsored project award implementations comply with federal, state, sponsor, and university requirements. Maintain productive relationships with sponsoring agencies, partner institutions, industry collaborators, and other external stakeholders. Award Set-up, Contracts, and Agreements Negotiations Oversee award intake, review, negotiation, set-up, and handoff processes to ensure awards are established accurately and efficiently. Lead or supervise contract and agreement negotiations related to sponsored programs, including grants, contracts, subawards, data use agreements, confidentiality agreements, material transfer agreements, and other research-related agreements as appropriate. Coordinate with the Office of General Counsel, academic units, principal investigators, sponsors, and external partners to resolve contractual, regulatory, financial, and operational issues. Support private sector and external collaborations by ensuring that sponsored project agreements are structured to protect the university while enabling timely, productive partnerships. Oversee processing of post-award program reporting and authorization of project change actions. Post-award Reporting and Financial Administration Support Oversee post-award financial administration, including financial system fund setup, sponsor reporting, invoicing, financial monitoring, effort and cost-share tracking and reporting support, budget revisions, expenditure review, and closeout. Ensure sponsored project financial activity is accurate, timely, compliant, and aligned with sponsor terms and institutional, federal and State requirements. Provide leadership for financial reporting, analysis, forecasting, and issue resolution related to sponsored projects. Partner with principal investigators, departments, colleges, finance offices, and central administration to address financial questions and support responsible project management. Research Administration Infrastructure and Continuous Improvement Lead efforts to strengthen institutional research administration infrastructure through the development of policies, procedures, guidelines, best practices, and service standards. Collaborate with ORI units, Finance, General Counsel, Human Resources, Information Technology, academic colleges, and other campus partners to improve interdependent business processes and support research growth. Identify opportunities to leverage technology, automation, and data-informed decision-making to improve operational effectiveness. Ensure the maintenance, integrity, and reporting of sponsored project data and records for institutional leadership and external stakeholders. Customer Service, Outreach, and Training Foster a highly responsive, service-oriented culture that supports faculty, staff, administrators, and external sponsors while maintaining appropriate institutional oversight. Facilitate communication and problem-solving among colleges, principal investigators, research administrators, and financial staff to improve processes and address operational challenges. Develop and deliver training, educational programs, guidance materials, and workshops related to sponsored programs administration, financial management, and compliance. Promote a campus culture that supports responsible growth in sponsored research, scholarship, creative activities, and innovation. Personnel Leadership and Staff Development Supervise, mentor, and evaluate CGA staff and provide overall leadership for a staff of approximately 20 employees. Recruit, develop, and retain highly qualified staff committed to excellence in service, compliance, and operational effectiveness. Empower staff to exercise sound judgment, solve problems proactively, and assume ownership of assigned responsibilities. Promote professional development, succession planning, workload management, and continuous learning across the unit. Foster a collaborative, solutions-oriented, and professional team culture grounded in accountability, continuous improvement, compliance, and service. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday - Friday 8:00 - 5:00 pm in-person Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $133,276 - $138,000 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date 09/27/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/07/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 11/02/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Resume List of References with Contact Information Finalists will be subject to a criminal background check prior to the offer of employment. All candidate names and information will remain confidential; however, finalists invited to campus may be asked to waive confidentiality to engage with the broader campus community. References will not be contacted without a candidate’s prior knowledge and consent. Search Chair Name Christine Hendren Search Chair Email hendrenco@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55912 Posting Number 201501836P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/52525": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Studio Art Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Studio Art Adjunct Instructor Pool Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Studio Art Adjunct Instructor Pool Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter — the letter should include a list of which Graphic Design courses you would be qualiﬁed to teach and what your approach to those courses would be. Curriculum vitae List of references with contact information Sample teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, previous teaching evaluations) are encouraged but not required upon initial application. Ofﬁcial transcripts will be required at a later stage of hire consideration. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Studio Art Adjunct Instructor Pool Department Art - 265050 Location Boone, NC Position Number 018863 Description of Department The Department of Art is accredited by NASAD and has 47 full-time faculty members, over 20 part-time faculty members, over 800 undergraduate majors and offers the following degrees: BFAs in Art Education, Graphic Design, Photography with concentrations in Commercial and Fine Art, and Studio Art; a BA in Art & Visual Culture with concentrations in Art History, Art Management and Studio Art; and a BS in Graphic Communications Management with concentrations in Cross Media Production and Print/Packaging Production. The Department of Art typically offers a range of travel opportunities, including trips to the university’s New York Loft and has offered study abroad trips to China, Costa Rica, Cuba, Italy, Japan, the Netherlands, Scotland, Spain, and Taiwan. Additional information about the department, the university, and the surrounding area can be found at art.appstate.edu. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or related discipline or BFA in Graphic Design with extensive professional experience. Essential Job Functions The Department of Art seeks to hire multiple adjunct instructors for various courses in graphic design for Spring 2026 and the academic year 2026-27. Instruction may be face-to-face or online, depending on need. Essential job functions include course preparation and delivery, grading, student engagement, and weekly ofﬁce hours. Instructors are expected to submit materials for departmental and/or General Education assessment as requested by the department chair. Courses taught may include: ART 1102: Introduction to Graphic Design ART 2102: Typography I ART 3102: Typography II ART 3202: Interaction Design I ART 3302: Sign, Symbol, Image ART 4102: Typography III ART 3602: Special Topics in Graphic Design Other courses depending on department need and instructor expertise are welcome. Applicants may also propose a topic not currently included among those listed in the course catalog (please see the list of courses for Graphic Design ). Preferred Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or related discipline Relevant teaching experience Experience teaching online asynchronous courses Number of Hours Per Week Variable Number of Months per Year 9 Hiring Range Commensurate with qualifications and equity Posting Details Posting Date 10/30/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire 01/12/2026 Evaluation of Applications Begins 11/13/2023 Search Chair Name Mark Nystrom Search Chair Email nystromml@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter — the letter should include a list of which Graphic Design courses you would be qualiﬁed to teach and what your approach to those courses would be. Curriculum vitae List of references with contact information Sample teaching materials (syllabi, assignments, previous teaching evaluations) are encouraged but not required upon initial application. Ofﬁcial transcripts will be required at a later stage of hire consideration. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which of the following best describes your interest and experience teaching fully online courses? I am not interested in teaching online courses I am interested in teaching online courses, but I have no previous experience. I have previous experience teaching online courses and would be interested in teaching online for App State Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Link to Portfolio Sample Syllabus Evidence of Teaching Teaching Evaluations & Peer Reviews Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/47423": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Athletic Trainer/Injury Clinic Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Athletic Trainer/Injury Clinic Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach required document: Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest (optional) List of references with contact information (optional) List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application or attach a List of References with Contact Information Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Athletic Trainer/Injury Clinic Location Boone, NC Position Number N32400 Department Health Services - 320000 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Maintains current NATABOC certification, North Carolina Licensure and current Adult CPR / AED certification. Successful completion of an accredited training program. License/Certification Required Maintains current NATABOC certification, North Carolina Licensure and current Adult CPR / AED certification. Essential Job Functions Provide services that include evaluation, treatment and rehabilitation of students. These services may include injuries, post-operative rehab, or non-injury orthopedic problems. Work cooperatively and effectively with clinicians on staff. Maintain and complete medical records in a timely fashion. Attend administrative conferences, in-service and continuing education programs. Act as a consultant for student health promotions, research projects and academic courses when requested. Accept other assignments as delegated by the Director. Preferred Qualifications Post-graduate and student health experience. Work Schedule/Hours 8:00 am – 5:00 pm Monday – Friday Number of Hours Per Week 20 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Light work. Exert up to 20 lbs of force occasionally, & or up to 10 lbs of force frequently & or a trivial amount of force constantly to move object. Light work if use of arm & or leg controls require exertion greater than sedentary and required to sit most of the time. Hiring Range Dependent upon experience Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 09/07/2022 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach required document: Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest (optional) List of references with contact information (optional) List a minimum of 3 professional references in the application or attach a List of References with Contact Information Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/33196 Posting Number 201500477P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
