    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55711": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Simulation Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Simulation Operations Specialist Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Simulation Operations Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must submit the below items to be considered: Resume / CV Cover Letter List of References with contact info Two (2) Letters of Recommendation Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Technology Support Analyst Working Title Simulation Operations Specialist Location Boone, NC Job Category 3 Position Number 099861 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Department of Nursing - 273300 Primary Purpose of Position The Simulation Operations Specialist is responsible for assisting the Department of Nursing in Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences in all related healthcare simulation labs, simulation activities, and innovative educational practices related to healthcare simulation technologies. In collaboration with the Director of Healthcare Simulation & Innovative Learning, the Simulation Operations Specialist will contribute by providing a safe, confidential, and welcoming learning simulation learning experience to the Department of Nursing programs as well as other internal and external stakeholders. Minimum Qualifications Graduation from a two year technical college with a major in computer science, information technology or related area and one year in the information technology field related to the position’s role; or graduation from a four year college or university and one year experience in the information technology field related to the position’s role; or graduation from a four year college or university with a major in computer science or information technology or related degree. Related information technology experience may be substituted year for year for the required education. Degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required Preferred Certifications: Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator® (CHSE®) certification; Certified Healthcare Simulation Operations Specialist® (CHSOS®) certification; Essential Job Functions Job Duties & Responsibilities include: Providing daily operation, maintenance and upgrades for clinical and simulation equipment; Maintaining sim and lab inventory; requiring a high degree of autonomy and independent judgment; Excellent interpersonal skills to work with faculty, staff and students in simulation experiences; Developing, implementing and evaluating protocols and policies related to simulation and learning lab operations under the direction of and in collaboration with the Simulation Director; In collaboration with the Simulation Director, schedule regular site visits with external vendors for troubleshooting and regular equipment maintenance and updates. Maintain a current, complete, and accurate inventory of all clinical laboratory equipment and supplies. Assist with the regular purchasing and documentation of all simulation equipment and lab supplies, in collaboration with lab faculty and the Simulation Director. Facilitate training sessions to ensure that faculty members are knowledgeable to provide basic operation of all clinical equipment. Collect and analyze data related to simulation usage and evaluation. In collaboration with the Simulation Director, submit annual outcome and evaluation reports of lab utilization and activity. Operate both simulators and AV recording equipment during student learning and faculty training scenarios. Set up and maintain labs as needed by internal and external stakeholders. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Ability to troubleshoot basic hardware/software issues Accomplished using Microsoft Office Suite and Adobe Media Products Excellent written and verbal communication skills Knowledge of and experience with patient simulation equipment and related multimedia equipment Familiarity with basic anatomy and physiology Ability to understand basic inventory and material storage procedures Knowledge of relevant health professions principles and practices Ability to safely operate common medical equipment and associated resources Understanding and application of universal precautions when working with biological materials This position must have a knowledge base about the technology associated with simulation lab training. In addition, the position must have a broad understanding of the simulation lab technical systems, including computer hardware and software, LAN equipment and switching/signaling, networking, server-client relationships, A/V equipment. Support experience with high-fidelity human patient simulators and other simulation-related technology is especially important for this position. Preferred Qualifications At least 1-year experience with health-related learning technology/simulation; Experience with video capture and learning management systems ( LMS ) software package (e.g., CAE Learning Space, B-Line); Experience in higher education; Relevant clinical experience and or/medical knowledge. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Technical Support This position should have the ability to identify trends and make suggestions for technical modifications to solve future problems. This person works collaboratively with the Director of Healthcare Simulation & Innovation, faculty, and other existing technology support team members. They will respond to simulation lab technical service requests, and must be available to assist faculty and students by providing simulation instructional technology support. Technical Solution Development This position will document and clearly articulate solutions. This position must also be able to organize and develop ad hoc support plans and direct efforts to quickly resolve unforeseen, immediate issues. The simulation labs are in continual operation and equipment uptime is critical. This position is responsible for developing support solutions to ensure that the labs training environment is consistently available for students and instructors. This position is expected to think strategically and creatively and to develop technical support protocols that provide optimal lab functionality and availability. Technical Knowledge This position must have a knowledge base about the technology associated with simulation lab training. In addition, the position must have a broad understanding of the simulation lab technical systems, including computer hardware and software, LAN equipment and switching/signaling, networking, server-client relationships, A/V equipment. Support experience with high-fidelity human patient simulators and other simulation-related technology is especially important for this position. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday – Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm. There may be times when it is necessary to work beyond the normal work schedule, but this is very rarely. Number of Hours Per Week Monday – Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm. There may be occasional times when it is necessary to work beyond the normal work schedule. Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position Physical demands involve activities associated with working with computers and other related technology. The work is not stationary and requires active involvement. Moderate lifting and moving of simulation equipment when/if necessary. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Overall Competency Level Contributing Salary Grade Equivalency IT01 Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $50,557 - $53,000 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/03/2026 Closing Date 09/20/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must submit the below items to be considered: Resume / CV Cover Letter List of References with contact info Two (2) Letters of Recommendation Search Chair Name Jennifer White Search Chair Email whitejm20@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55539 Posting Number 201503028P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letter of Recommendation (1st doc) List of References with Contact Information Letter of Recommendation (2nd doc) Optional Documents Transcript-Associate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Curriculum Vitae Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54428": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Associate Director of On-Campus Recruiting",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Associate Director of On-Campus Recruiting Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Associate Director of On-Campus Recruiting Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit the following required documents: Resume Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Associate Director of On-Campus Recruiting Location Boone, North Carolina Faculty Rank No Provide Rank Position Number 091121 Department Football - 120050 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Athletics Department provides a dynamic environment where passionate professionals come to make an impact. The Recruiting Division for Football plays a uniquely important role in the success of Appalachian State University’s Football program. The unit assists the football program with player acquisition and roster management. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Knowledge of the NCAA rules and regulations related to recruiting and working with student-athletes Exceptional interpersonal and counseling skills Experience with recruiting student-athletes Experience working within an NCAA FBS football program License/Certification Required Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Associate Director of On-Campus Recruiting assists the Head Football Coach and Director of On-Campus Recruiting with the planning of official and unofficial visits, coordinating recruiting events, and handling daily administrative and operational tasks within the football program. Some of the responsibilities are: Assist with the preparation and execution of recruiting visits and events. Oversee the preparation and organization of all physical materials for recruiting visits and events. Assist with coordinating vendors for recruiting visits and events. Assist with keeping the Recruiting Operations Calendar up to date. Oversee the Recruiting Operations Internship Program. Track, organize, and manage all recruiting-related receipts and financial documentation for accurate reconciliation and budget tracking. Complete post-official visit paperwork required for NCAA compliance, including submission of receipts, itineraries, and verification forms to the Compliance Office. Plan and manage all travel arrangements for coaching staff during recruiting trips. Manage inventory and ordering of all recruiting visit/event supplies, ensuring materials are stocked, organized, and available for events, visits, and daily operations. Assist with High School Relations. Additional tasks as assigned. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Mon-Fri, 8:00-5:00 pm except when traveling. Evening, weekend and holiday work is required Number of Hours Per Week 40+ Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 05/26/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 05/26/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 06/15/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit the following required documents: Resume Search Chair Name Ethan Baxter Search Chair Email baxterem@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54409 Posting Number 201501782P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
