    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/52588": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Group Fitness Class Instructor",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Group Fitness Class Instructor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Group Fitness Class Instructor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Group Fitness Class Instructor Location Boone, NC Position Number N36602 Department Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness - 273600 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Demonstrate ability to communicate effectively with diverse levels of education and fitness knowledge; Experience teaching group exercise classes to a wide variety of populations. Working knowledge of human anatomy, kinesiology, and training principles; Knowledge of group fitness teaching strategies and incorporation of music, temp technique, and rhythm; Choreography and music skills; Ability to be professional and motivate class participants; and  Ability to colaborate and work well with other staff members License/Certification Required Must be willing to obtain an inhouse AHA HEartsaver certification and participate in monthly emergency action training. Essential Job Functions Teaches scheduled classes beginning and ending on time, provides adequate warm‐up, exercises, stretching, and cool down; Instructs participants on effective workout methods; explains proper techniques, demonstrates exercises; Identifies muscle groups, and teaches appropriate methods to strength specific muscles; Prepares appropriate equipment, music for participants; Assists participants, answers questions, and maintains a positive exercise experience for class participants; Keeps management informed of participant and facility needs; Ensures that safety standards are met, and that department and facility policies are adhered to; While performing the duties of this job, the employee occasionally will work with various types of fitness equipment; The noise level in the work environment is generally loud within the facility and while performing duties. Preferred Qualifications Group Class instructor or acquire within 6 months of accepting the position. Work Schedule/Hours Hours and schedule depend on number of classes taught. Number of Hours Per Week 1-15 hours per week Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $15.00-$20.00/hr Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 11/07/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/52585 Posting Number 201500963P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
