      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Accountant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Accountant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. submit resume Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Accountant Location Boone, NC Position Number N28912 Department Contracts and Grants Accounting - 415102 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Graduation from high school, with at least 5 years of related accounting experience; graduation from a four-year college or university and 1 year of related accounting experience, or an equivalent combination of training and experience. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Process incoming transactions according to CGA , University, State of NC, and federal guidelines, policies and regulations. Analysis, data entry, filing. Grant administration projects as assigned by Director, or Assistant Director of Contracts and Grants Accounting. Preferred Qualifications 10 years accounting related experience. Work Schedule/Hours Flexible, generally within the hours of Monday – Friday, 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Number of Hours Per Week up to 20 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $30 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/14/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants submit resume Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54954 Posting Number 201500124P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
