    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55772": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Food Service Technician",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Food Service Technician Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Food Service Technician Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Food Services Technician-ASU Working Title Food Service Technician Location Boone, NC Job Category 8 Position Number 037801 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Campus Dining - Bake Shop - 170360 Primary Purpose of Position The Cook is responsible for preparing high-quality meals in accordance with campus dining standards, recipes, and safety protocols. This role supports the kitchen team by ensuring food is prepared efficiently, safely, and attractively, while maintaining a clean and organized work environment. The Cook works under the direction of the Sous Chef and Chef de Cuisine and contributes to a positive dining experience for students, staff, and guests. Minimum Qualifications Experience in food preparation or service activities in a commercial kitchen; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all functions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Campus Dining has an immediate opening for a Food Service Technician. This entry-level job is a GREAT way to start a career with App State! Starting wages now surpass national averages by almost 10%. Campus Dining at Appalachian State University seek bright, energetic, and hard-working people to join our team and the Appalachian community! Awesome Benefits: All Campus Dining employees receive the benefit of the employee meal plan. This plan provides employees with two meals per 8-hour shift for $17.33 per month. (Meals must be taken during scheduled work hours, no take-home meals are permitted, and certain item restrictions apply.) Appalachian provides comprehensive benefit programs that are an essential part of one’s total compensation and are designed to provide income security for future needs, assist with meeting the costs of health care, and provide generous program of paid time off to help balance the demands of work and family. The tuition waiver and academic assistance program is also valuable educational benefit that can be used to further your professional and personal development. Opportunities in Dining Services at Appalachian State University are not just normal job opportunities, they are career opportunities! They are excellent starting points to fulfill and develop your career goals and passions. Our University is committed to seeking talented and aspiring employees who will contribute to our dynamic working environment. Our campus atmosphere is stimulating and supportive and is a place where both professional and personal development is encouraged and recognized. Come join us, apply today! NOTE : All ASU Food Service employees are required to work during home football games or any other special campus event as needed. Campus work location may vary depending on the event. The main purpose of the Food Service Technician in Campus Dining is to perform a variety of recurring tasks and functions related to assigned processes and procedures. Specific duties included, but are not limited to, Anticipate, identify, and understanding of customer service needs Maintain good rapport with customers while assisting them with obtaining desired products Check with customers and/or vendors to ensure products meet needs Establish and maintain good relationships with the community, faculty, staff, students, co-workers, and vendors Knowledge of food service sanitation principles This is non-skilled work in the food service operations of a state institution Employees assist in the preparation and serving of food, busing tables, ability to operate a register, and washing dishes Employees assist in the cleaning of the facility to ensure good sanitation and food service Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Knowledge Basic cooking techniques : Grilling, sautéing, roasting, baking, etc. Food safety and sanitation practices : Including temperature control, storage methods ( FIFO ), and cleanliness standards. Standardized recipes and portion control : Ability to follow and execute recipes accurately. Skills Food preparation and cooking : Efficiently prepare and cook meals with consistency in taste and presentation. Station setup and organization : Prepare workstations with necessary tools and safety items. Communication : Clearly communicate with team members about prep needs, timing, and dietary requests. Teamwork : Collaborate effectively with kitchen staff, student employees, and supervisors. Inventory awareness : Monitor supplies and ingredients, assist with deliveries and storage. Customer service : Present food professionally and interact courteously with students and staff. Abilities Follow instructions and recipes accurately . Work in a fast-paced environment and stand for extended periods. Lift up to 50 lbs and handle hot equipment and sharp tools safely. Maintain a clean and safe workstation throughout the shift. Support a respectful and inclusive kitchen culture . Preferred Qualifications Prefer someone with knowledge or experience in institutional baking. The ability to multi-task and work in a high production setting. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Knowledge/Technical Ability to follow standardized recipes and production sheets Reads menus correctly to estimate food requirements and procures food from storage Customer Service Responds to requests from fellow employees promptly and courteously Anticipates customer needs while being attentive to duties Safety and sanitation Practices good personal hygiene Foods stored according to state helath laws Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Campus Dining is a Sunday – Saturday, 7:00 am – 11:00 pm operation. Employees are scheduled two days off each week based on business need. Days off may not be consecutive days off. Cook – AM - 6:00 am – 3:00 pm typically scheduled days Cook – PM - 2:30 pm – 11:30 pm typically scheduled days Actual schedule times may vary. Operations are reduced during university breaks. Employees may be required to work some flex hours to support the needs of the business and/or for special campus events. Schedules will be adjusted as needed to provide coverage in these cases. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Medium work. Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Overall Competency Level Advanced Salary Grade Equivalency Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $36,816 - $37,400 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/29/2026 Closing Date 09/06/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Search Chair Name Jules Bott Search Chair Email Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55423 Posting Number 201503018P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54577": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Critical Minerals and Environmental Geochemistry",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Critical Minerals and Environmental Geochemistry Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor of Critical Minerals and Environmental Geochemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor of Critical Minerals and Environmental Geochemistry Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 0A0301 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Geological and Environmental Sciences - 250350 Working Location (City, State) Boone, North Carolina Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications The candidate must have a Ph.D. in geology, geoscience, environmental science, or a closely related field at the time of appointment. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications  (No Minimum Level Required) We are seeking a candidate whose research broadly covers critical minerals and low-temperature/aqueous geochemistry. A strong commitment to undergraduate education, mentoring undergraduate research, and developing an externally funded research program is desired. License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Geological and Environmental Sciences at Appalachian State University is undergraduate-only with 22 faculty members and more than 300 students majoring in geology or environmental science. The Department and the College of Arts and Sciences possess an array of analytical and field equipment that supports faculty and student research. More information about the Department is available on our website (https://earth.appstate.edu). Appalachian State is a comprehensive R2 university located in the Blue Ridge Mountains of western North Carolina and is a member of the University of North Carolina System. Essential Duties and Responsibilities This candidate will develop and teach upper-level undergraduate courses on: 1) critical minerals, and 2) aqueous or environmental geochemistry. Additional teaching responsibilities may include supporting one or more existing courses such as: Global Biogeochemical Cycles ( GES 3310), introductory lectures and/or labs, or research/field methods classes ( GES 2750/2751/2752), depending on the candidate’s area of expertise. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/16/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: No ABD consideration (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants To be considered, applications must include: A cover letter (maximum two pages) Curriculum vitae Teaching statement (maximum two pages, with emphasis on the courses to be taught), Statement of research interests (maximum two pages) Unofficial copies of transcripts of all college and university work (official copies due upon employment) The names and contact information (including e-mail) of three referees familiar with the applicant’s teaching and/or scholarship. Additional materials will not be considered in the review of applications. Questions about the position can be directed to Dr. Sarah Carmichael, at 828-262-8471 or carmichaelsk@appstate.edu. Review of completed applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 05/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Sarah Carmichael Search Chair Email carmichaelsk@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53696 Posting Number FA00587P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Interests Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53544": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Communication Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Communication Adjunct Instructor Pool Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Communication Adjunct Instructor Pool Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must upload: Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae – current Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - if avaliable List of References with Contact Information – names, email addresses, and telephone contact information for three references Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Communication Adjunct Instructor Pool Department Communication - 265100 Location Boone or Hickory Campus, or online/remote Position Number 018864 Description of Department The Department of Communication employs more than 40 full-time faculty members dedicated to teaching more than 1,000 students who major in Advertising, Communication Studies, Electronic Media/Broadcasting, Digital Journalism, and Public Relations. The department is also home to multiple award-winning student organizations and student-run media outlets, which are open to all students on campus: The Appalachian news organization; AppTV; The Peel Literature and Arts Review; Second Story Media, a student-run communication agency; and WASU -FM radio, and the university’s intercollegiate debate team. Departmental staff members include three full-time media advisors and an engineer who manages the production equipment and studios used in the department. Learn more at https://communication.appstate.edu Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Communication or related discipline, or evidence of exceptional professional experience is required. Essential Job Functions The Department of Communication seeks to hire adjunct lecturers to cover courses as needed for upcoming semesters. Successful applicants will teach one or two courses within the following academic majors : Advertising, Communication Studies, Electronic Media/Broadcasting, Digital Journalism, and Public Relations. Instruction may be in person, on the Boone or Hickory campuses, online, or hybrid, depending on need. Essential functions include course preparation and delivery, grading, student engagement, and weekly office hours. You may view the full list of courses offered by the Department of Communication, along with course descriptions, in the Undergraduate Bulletin . At this time we are most interested in lecturers who can teach one or more of the following courses: COM 1200 – Thinking Through Communication COM 1300 – Journalism Matters: An Introduction to News Literacy and News Writing COM 2101 – Public Speaking COM 2316 – Audio Production COM 2325 – Public Relations Principles COM 3618 – Public Relations Writing COM 2610 – News Reporting and Writing COM 2612 – Electronic Media Newswriting COM 2700 – Foundations of Advertising COM 3010 – Media Graphics COM 3210 – Fact-Checking and Editing COM 3340 – Journalism Ethics and a Free Society COM 4420 – Multimedia Storytelling Preferred Qualifications n/a Number of Hours Per Week 10 Number of Months per Year 5 Hiring Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Posting Details Posting Date 10/02/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire 01/01/2026 Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/16/2025 Search Chair Name Matt Richards and Carolyn Edy Search Chair Email richardsms@appstate.edu   and     edycm@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must upload: Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae – current Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) – if avaliable List of References with Contact Information – names, email addresses, and telephone contact information for three references UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please tell us the types of courses you'd be most interested in teaching and whether you'd prefer to teach in person on the Boone or Hickory campuses, or online. Thank you. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
