    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55895": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Housekeeper (Multiple Vacancies) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Housekeeper (Multiple Vacancies) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Building Environmental Services Technician (Housing Operations) Working Title Housekeeper (Multiple Vacancies) Location Boone, NC Job Category 8 Position Number 036131 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department University Housing-Operations - 325100 Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this position is to maintain all residence halls at a high level of cleanliness and sanitation. Housekeeping staff are responsible for the proper maintenance and appearance of residence hall public areas such as lobbies, lounges, hallways, stairwells and elevators. Housekeepers also clean and sanitize bathrooms, distribute supplies, sweep, mop and wax floors. Minimum Qualifications Some knowledge of cleaning procedures, ability to follow instructions and to perform medium to heavy physical work; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Duties include performing cleaning such as sweeping, mopping, scrubbing, dusting using environmentally preferred cleaning agents for cleaning and disinfecting vacuuming as well as operating floor maintenance equipment stripping and waxing floor as needed keeping work areas in a clean and orderly condition communicating with fellow workers, guests and students in a manner that allows work to be completed and insures harmony and teamwork in the workplace demonstrating knowledge of safety hazards Working as part of a team during summer cleaning in a variety of duties as listed above, and other duties as assigned by supervisor. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Ability to perform a variety of duties to include all aspects of cleaning such as dusting, sweeping, mopping, window cleaning, carpet cleaning, operation of floor maintenance equipment, stripping & waxing floors, trash removal, restroom sanitation, supply ordering, etc. Basic computer skills such as communicating through email, ordering online supplies, submitting work order requests. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, skills and abilities to perform a variety of duties including all aspects of cleaning, sweeping, mopping, trash removal, restroom sanitation, etc. Basic computer skills to perform tasks such as email and supply ordering. Experience in operating floor maintenance equipment such as auto scrubber, high speed buffer, carpet extractor. Knowledge and experience in using a variety of cleaning products including “Green Cleaning” products. Maintain a valid driver’s license. Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Knowledge/Technical: Cleans the interior and exterior of buildings using the appropriate cleaning solutions and equipment. Interpersonal Skills : Develops and maintains effective working relationships with others in order to encourage and support communication and teamwork. Customer Service: Respectfully listens and responds to customer, student, staff and faculty needs promptly. Communication: Listens to co-workers and/or guests questions or identifies questions that need answering. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday – Friday, 7am to 4pm; May require occasional evening and weekend work. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Job requires moderate to heavy physical work loads, some of which may be repetitive. Bending, stooping, twisting, etc. as well as climbing step ladders Overall Competency Level Journey Salary Grade Equivalency Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $34,321 - $35,588 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/28/2026 Closing Date 09/13/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Search Chair Name Kerry Hines Search Chair Email hineske2@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55879 Posting Number 201503041P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
