    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56003": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Student Records Specialist",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Student Records Specialist Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Student Records Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: Cover Letter Resume List of three professional references with contact information included Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Administrative Support Specialist-Records Working Title Student Records Specialist Location Boone, NC Job Category 6 Position Number 022091 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department College of Fine and Applied Arts - 265000 Primary Purpose of Position The Student Records (Administrative Support) Specialist assists students by tracking their academic records of course work, performing senior checks, and completing graduation audits and degree clearances for students in the College. Other record-keeping tasks involving student academic records are also required (readmission and visiting coursework approval assistance, GPA calculations, forms processing, and change of program requests, etc.). Minimum Qualifications Graduation from high school and one year of related office experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all positions. Diplomas or degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions The Student Records Specialist position works in the Dean’s Office of the College of Fine and Applied Arts and has specifically defined areas of responsibility and works with the Dean to promote recognition of the College and plan College functions. The Student Records Specialist works to enhance, develop, and implement supportive academic services to the undergraduates in the College. In addition, they provide educational services to all students enrolled in all General Education courses offered by the College of Fine and Applied Arts. They maintain contact with the broader university constituency through participation by the staff on university committees and by presenting at workshops and training. The office staff responds to inquiries and concerns from students, faculty, administrators, and parents. Maintaining current knowledge and providing helpful information are standards expected of all office staff. Duties and Responsibilities include: Communicating information clearly to students, faculty, parents, staff, and administrators about services, processes, and procedures using prescribed or established guidelines. Applying judgment in releasing confidential information or to whom to refer questions. Maintaining FERPA compliance and assisting departments in doing so as well. Responsible for processing new major declarations and completing program changes, senior checks, and graduation audits for eligible CFAA students. Checks must be accurate and sent to all advisors and students promptly to ensure shortages are no surprises during the final semester at AppState. Communicating with other departments, such as the Registrar’s Office, regarding the status of student records and issues and/or the status of graduates (multiple times per year); updating Transfer Admissions and Engagement as needed regarding re-articulation issues; and updating academic departments with academic record updates (senior checks, substitutions, changes of major, etc.). Preparing and sending audits on demand to offices with higher-level needs, such as Financial Aid required course confirmation requests. Responding to emails/letters with specific issues regarding program requirements, such as program changes, substitutions, etc. Answering questions regarding audit results, such as GPA calculations, how substitutions affect earned hours, etc. Processing new major declaration notifications to departments, changes of program, and pre-graduation audits (senior checks). Reviewing all senior students’ applications for graduation certification (three times per year). Reviewing data and information for completeness and accuracy per academic policies and procedures. Demonstrating knowledge of academic policies and procedures regarding students’ records—the ability to answer questions regarding student academic information. Ability to access and interpret appropriate resources to answer questions about policies and/or procedures. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Knowledge of academic policies and procedures at AppState Thorough knowledge of all degree requirements, including majors, minors (inside and outside the College), and general education Ability to make judgments about and to incorporate changes/revisions to all the above policies, procedures, and requirements frequently Ability to do GPA calculations, including GPA projections based on current schedule Knowledge of and firm understanding of DegreeWorks logic, scribing, and reporting functions to make exceptions and adjust the individual curricula to provide students and faculty with correct information Excellent communication skills, both oral and written, as well as organizational and time management skills Ability to process large volumes of work in a short time frame to meet University deadlines Most of the time is allocated to tasks that involve several steps and require selecting the most appropriate action with procedural and operational guidelines Preferred Qualifications Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Communication – Written: Responsible for processing new major declarations and completing program changes, senior checks, and graduation audits for eligible CFAA students. Checks must be accurate and sent to all advisors and students promptly to ensure shortages are no surprises during the final semester at AppState. Prepares and emails correspondence to students who have applied for graduation (three times per year) concerning their graduation status/deficiencies while working within a time frame of a few weeks. Students with shortages are also contacted after commencement. Communicate with other departments, such as the Registrar’s Office, regarding the status of student records and issues and/or the status of graduates (multiple times per year); update Transfer Admissions and Engagement as needed regarding re-articulation issues; and update academic departments with academic record updates (senior checks, substitutions, changes of major, etc.). Prepares and sends audits on demand to offices with higher-level needs, such as Financial Aid required course confirmation requests. Responds to emails/letters with specific issues regarding program requirements, such as program changes, substitutions, etc. Answers questions regarding audit results, such as questions regarding GPA calculations, how substitutions affect earned hours, etc. Answers questions from faculty advisors regarding program changes, academic policies, and procedures. Responds to numerous questions regarding General Education, catalog year, residency requirements, transfer coursework, etc. While some procedural information is basic, most are FERPA -protected information dealing strictly with an individual student, and strict confidentiality must be maintained. Information/Records Administration: Processes new major declaration notifications to departments, changes of program, and pre-graduation audits (senior checks). Review all senior students’ applications for graduation certification (three times per year). Review data and information for completeness and accuracy per academic policies and procedures. Knowledge-Program: Understanding when interpretations, applications, and allowable exceptions of written policies and procedures for academic issues may be approved. Through training with the supervisor and others in the College and across the University, this staff person is responsible for understanding the organizational structure, functions, services, and programs of each academic area in the College. Staff members stay informed of changes and participate in on-campus training, the Undergraduate Advising Committee notes, and internal training sessions to remain current and serve as a resource for students and faculty. Demonstrates knowledge of academic policies and procedures regarding students’ records—the ability to answer questions regarding student academic information. Ability to access and interpret appropriate resources to answer questions about policies and/or procedures. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday through Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm, with occasional after-hours work required. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Overall Competency Level Advanced Salary Grade Equivalency GN06 Salary Range Anticipated Hiring Range $43,542- $48,042 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date 09/27/2026 Competency Level Statement If no applicants apply who meet the required competencies, then management may consider other applicants at a lower competency level. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: Cover Letter Resume List of three professional references with contact information included Search Chair Name Jason Miller Search Chair Email millerdj1@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56001 Posting Number 201503050P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience working in an academic and/or student services environment? (Response must be substantiated by employment history information on the application) Yes No * Briefly describe your experience with Banner Student, DegreeWorks, and Google Workspace products or related technologies. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
