    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/51756": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Temporary PRN Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Temporary PRN Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Temporary PRN Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Complete online application. Also submit CV and a list of 3 references. Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Temporary PRN Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant Location Boone, North Carolina Position Number N32400 Department Health Services - 320000 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Nurse Practitioner: Licensed as a Registered Nurse by the North Carolina Board of Nursing, graduation from a Nurse Practitioner program approved by the North Carolina Medical Board, and “approved to practice medical acts” consistent with the nurse practitioner’s academic educational preparation AND national certification. or Physician Assistant: Graduation and or completion of an educational program for Physician Assistants accredited by the Accreditation and Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant and an active Physician Assistant License issued by the North Carolina Medical Board. NCCPA certification needed. License/Certification Required As detailed in “Minimum Qualifications”. Also an unrestricted DEA license is required. Also, “Dispensing License” from the North Carolina Board of Pharmacy may be required. Essential Job Functions The Mary S. Shook Student Health Service exists to provide for the health care needs of the students of Appalachian State University. This position provides patient care, including performing assessment, determining diagnosis, developing treatment plans, prescribing medication, engaging in research activities, and providing training and education for a wide variety of medical conditions under the supervision of a physician. This position will also participate in continuous quality improvement and accreditation programs at health services. Perform medical acts within his/her area of educational preparation and certification under a collaborative practice agreement ( CPA ), with a licensed physician. Ability to manage complex dilemmas. Ability to anticipate, recognize and respond to potentially problematic situations. Knowledge of advanced communication techniques. Skill in observing behavior and mannerisms. Ability to actively listen. Ability to answer questions from healthcare personnel and patients on diseases processes, diagnosis and treatment. Ability to diagnose mental health illnesses and to treat them appropriately. Ability to interpret lab tests, EKG’s, and xrays. Ability to coordinate referrals to specialists. Work with other agencies on campus in the prevention of illnesses and care of illnesses and care of students who become ill or injured. Provide health education to individuals or to groups on campus in order to promote optimal health and prevent future illness. Coordinate and monitor the CQI and accreditation programs at the Student Health Service. Working knowledge of patient care practices and held accountable for the continuous and comprehensive management of a broad range of personal health services for which the nurse practitioner/physician assistant is educationally prepared and for which competency has been maintained. These services include but are not restricted to: (1) promotion and maintenance of health; (2) prevention of illness and disability; (3) diagnosing, treating and managing acute and chronic illnesses; (4) guidance and counseling for both individuals and families; (5) prescribing, administering and dispensing therapeutic measures, tests, procedures and drugs; (6) planning for situations beyond their expertise and consulting with and referring to other health care providers as appropriate; and (7) evaluating health outcomes. Preferred Qualifications Although general medicine knowledge is required, training and/or experience with adolescent medical care is also highly desirable. Sports medicine knowledge is also desirable. Work Schedule/Hours This would be a temporary as needed position to help supplement the work of full time clinicians. The PRN employee might fill in when full time clinicians are out on sick or vacation leave. The PRN employee might work during especially busy clinic times. Student Health has some limited weekend clinic hours and there may be need for PRN weekend coverage at times, too. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $50/hour Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 12/07/2018 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Complete online application. Also submit CV and a list of 3 references. Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/20480 Posting Number 201500437P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation (1st doc) Letter of Recommendation (2nd doc) Letter of Recommendation (3rd doc) Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55790": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Project Manager, Rural Health Transformation Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Project Manager, Rural Health Transformation Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a grant-funded, time-limited position supporting implementation of the North Carolina Rural Health Transformation Program in Region 3. Continued employment is contingent upon continued funding, satisfactory performance, and University approval. Final classification, salary, reporting line, and appointment terms are subject to App State Human Resources review. Applicants should submit a resume, cover letter/letter of interest, and a list of three professional references with contact information. Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Project Manager, Rural Health Transformation Location Boone, North Carolina Faculty Rank Provide Rank Position Number 0A1141 Department Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness - 273600 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Rural Health Transformation Program Manager provides senior leadership for Appalachian State University’s Region 3 rural health career-services and workforce-pathway portfolio. The position designs and directs career development, experiential learning, employer engagement, participant support, placement, and retention strategies; supervises career-services professionals; and ensures that regional programs connect education and training to rural employment. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in career services, higher education, counseling, workforce development, education, public health, health sciences, healthcare administration, human resources, or a related field. At least five years of progressively responsible professional experience in career services, workforce development, employer engagement, experiential learning, cooperative education, apprenticeships, clinical or field education, healthcare workforce, public health workforce, or related student and trainee programs. License/Certification Required Preferred Qualifications Experience leading complex programs involving students or trainees, employers, educational institutions, healthcare providers, public agencies, or community partners. Experience supervising or providing professional direction to staff. Demonstrated ability to design and manage career pathways, experiential-learning programs, employer partnerships, placement processes, or workforce initiatives. Strong skills in program leadership, advising, facilitation, consultation, problem-solving, writing, training, data interpretation, evaluation, and relationship management. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Lead and coordinate Appalachian State University’s Region 3 rural health career-services and workforce-pathway portfolio, including Scholars, Fellows, apprenticeships, paid work-based learning, clinical and field placements, rural rotations, residency pathways, certificate programs, and other approved student and trainee initiatives. Design and maintain education-to-workforce pathways that connect students and trainees with rural health employers, training sites, and career opportunities. Direct employer and training-site engagement, including development of experiential-learning opportunities, site-readiness processes, supervision and preceptor supports, participant placement, and transition-to-employment strategies. Supervise Technical Assistance Specialists and coordinate their assigned participant, employer, provider, community, and training-site portfolios. Coordinate with the Rural Health Workforce Partnerships Manager and Workforce Pathways and Cooperative Programs Coordinator to align cooperative education, placements, apprenticeships, employer engagement, and participant-support processes. Establish consistent participant advising, eligibility, placement, follow-up, service-commitment, and retention processes within approved program requirements. Monitor participant, employer, training-site, placement, completion, credential, transition-to-employment, and retention outcomes; identify barriers and recommend program improvements. Develop and maintain career-services resources, pathway tools, employer and supervisor guidance, orientation materials, training, and implementation supports. Coordinate regional workforce activities with App State, Vaya Health, AHEC , educational institutions, employers, public health agencies, and other approved partners. Maintain required program documentation, monitor progress toward approved deliverables, and support required reporting and continuous improvement. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours 800-500 pm Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $75,000-$80,000 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/24/2026 Closing Date 09/07/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 08/26/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 09/15/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants This is a grant-funded, time-limited position supporting implementation of the North Carolina Rural Health Transformation Program in Region 3. Continued employment is contingent upon continued funding, satisfactory performance, and University approval. Final classification, salary, reporting line, and appointment terms are subject to App State Human Resources review. Applicants should submit a resume, cover letter/letter of interest, and a list of three professional references with contact information. Search Chair Name Alex Howard Search Chair Email howardaf@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55789 Posting Number 201501832P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53824": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Express To Go Technician",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Express To Go Technician Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Express To Go Technician Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Express To Go Technician Location Boone, NC Position Number N32340 Department Campus Dining - Sanford Commons - 170380 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Experience in food preparation or service activities in a commercial kitchen; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. [Special Requirements may apply for individual positions such as certification requirements by Department of Correction.] Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but may not be applicable to all functions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Work in this class involves the preparation and serving of food in a state facility. Duties include food preparation, to include large scale cooking and/or baking of a wide variety of food products and/or table service to customers in the dining area. Duties also include kitchen, service area, and dining room sanitation and cleaning as required by Health and Sanitation good practices. Employees in this class may also serve as a lead worker over subordinate staff including students assigned to the foodservice operation. Work is performed in accordance with menus prepared and quantities needed based on projected business as approved and monitored by a supervisor. Foodservice skill is required in determining cooking times for the various food items in order to complete all aspects of the meal at the appropriate serving time and temperature. Work is performed under close supervision by a higher-level food service employee and is reviewed regularly for successful completion of assignments. Duties may also include serving food and beverages to customers while displaying consistent and appropriate serving etiquette, and merchandizing products or displaying items attractively. Employees record menus and convey food orders to customers and other production staff. Employees serve prepared food and drinks providing continuous service to customers. Employees may also operate a dish machine or clear dishes and trays from tables or dining rooms following each meal and present customers with their check. Accountability and accuracy is expected when handling money from customers or vending machines. Adherence of North Carolina ABC Licensure Laws is expected. Employees also perform any other responsible task as requested by a supervisor. Preferred Qualifications N/A Work Schedule/Hours Campus Dining is a Sunday – Saturday, 6:00 am – 11:00 pm operation. Employees are scheduled two days off each week based on business need. Days off may not be consecutive days off. Actual schedule times may vary. Employees may be required to work some flex hours to support the needs of the business and/or for special campus events. Schedules will be adjusted as needed to provide coverage in these cases. Number of Hours Per Week 30 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Lifting items over 40 lbs. Stooping and bending to retrieve items from ovens, shelves, etc. Sweeping and mopping area each day. Scrubbing and cleaning of all equipment daily. This employee is required to stand on your feet for your entire 8-hour shift. Hiring Range $14 - $18.88 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 11/26/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/52644 Posting Number 201501024P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55907": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Staff Counselor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Staff Counselor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vita / Resume List of References with Contact Information Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Staff Counselor Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank Position Number 001221 Department Counseling Center & Psychological Services - 315100 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose In general, the duties expected of a staff counselor are to contribute to the mission of the Counseling & Psychological Services Center by participating in all areas of service delivery. Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Counseling, Social Work, or related field, and eligibility for appropriate licensure in North Carolina. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain licensure for the continuation of the appointment. License/Certification Required Master’s Degree in Counseling, Social Work, or related field, and eligibility for appropriate licensure in North Carolina (e.g. Licensed Clinical Mental Health Counselor / LCMHCA , Licensed Clinical Social Worker / LCSWA ). The successful candidate will be expected to obtain licensure in North Carolina within one month of start date and maintain licensure for the continuation of the appointment. Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience in a university counseling center with a student affairs perspective. 2. Demonstrated interest, skill, and experience in one of the following areas: Interest and experience in providing clinical services and outreach programming to student populations who may be less likely to seek counseling. Interest and experience in using a variety of methods for engaging students to support their mental health, such as innovative outreach and development of self-help resources. Candidates should also be committed to a proactive student development perspective involving an active relationship with the campus community; have demonstrated skills and interest in working with students from a wide range of backgrounds and identities; be team-oriented and collaborative with students, colleagues, and university staff; and have broad generalist clinical skills in assessing and intervening with a wide range of disorders, concerns, and degrees of pathology. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Duties of the position include: short-term individual and couples therapy; group therapy; psychological assessment; crisis intervention; consultation; outreach and psychoeducational workshops (sometimes after hours); case management as needed; liaison/consultant relationships with university partners; rotating after hours emergency/crisis on call responsibilities as back-up to ProtoCall. administrative duties and roles based on interest / experience and the needs of the Counseling Center. Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Mon-Fri, 8:00 A.M.-5:00 P.M. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Physical Demands of Position Posting Details Information Posting Date 04/08/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 04/27/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 07/20/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach required documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vita / Resume List of References with Contact Information Search Chair Name Julie Keys Search Chair Email keysj@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/53769 Posting Number 201501757P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Resume Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
