      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Part Time Special Faculty of Marketing - Boone Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Part Time Special Faculty of Marketing - Boone Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter ● CV ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Part Time Special Faculty of Marketing - Boone Department Marketing & Supply Chain Mgmt (SCM) - 255350 Location Boone, NC Position Number 006818 Description of Department Marketing & Supply Chain Management is currently the largest department (in terms of undergraduate degree seeking students) of six departments within the John A. Walker College of Business. Business students may choose from three marketing concentrations – General Marketing, Digital Marketing or Professional Selling. The department also offers minors in professional selling (for business majors), sales (for non-business majors) and general marketing (for non-business majors). Additionally, business students can also earn a Supply Chain Management major or minor. Graduate level courses are offered in the MBA / MS in Analytics program. The Marketing & Supply Chain Management Department consists of 16 tenured/ tenure track and 11 adjunct faculty members. The Walker College of Business is one of the largest public business schools for undergraduate students in the University of North Carolina system. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Marketing or MBA Essential Job Functions The person who fills this position will be expected to provide instruction primarily in the following areas of Digital Marketing, General Marketing and Professional Selling Instructional duties will include a teaching load of up to six credit hours per semester and participation in curriculum development. Location of this position is Boone Campus. In addition to instructional duties, faculty members will be expected to contribute to service activities such as alumni relations, participation in student recruiting activities, and other departmental activities. Preferred Qualifications The department is especially interested in candidates with teaching interests in one or more of the following areas – Digital Marketing, General Marketing and/or Professional Selling. Number of Hours Per Week TBD - Part Time, Semester to Semester Number of Months per Year 9 Hiring Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Posting Details Posting Date 05/13/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire Evaluation of Applications Begins 05/13/2024 Search Chair Name Stephanie J. Lawson Search Chair Email lawsonsj1@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter ● CV ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
