    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55028": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Lecturers Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Lecturers Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: 1. Letter of Interest/Cover Letter that includes interest in teaching and teaching-related experience. 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. List of References with Contact Information 4. A copy of unofficial graduate degree transcripts Official transcripts will be requested later. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Lecturers Department Social Work - 273500 Location Boone, NC and/or remote in North Carolina Position Number 085836 Description of Department Housed within the Beaver College of Health Sciences, the Department of Social Work at Appalachian State University is guided by an overarching framework of social and economic justice. The mission of the Department of Social Work is to educate professional social workers who actively work towards a sustainable and just society. We partner with Appalachian and global communities to advance social, economic, and environmental justice for all people. The undergraduate ( BSW ) and graduate ( MSW ) programs are designed to assist competent generalist social work practice within the distinct Appalachian culture of the region and across national and international contexts. Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s in Social Work ( MSW ) and at least two years post master’s experience. Essential Job Functions Essential job functions include course preparation and delivery, maintaining office hours, grading, and student engagement. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching in higher education Expertise: Research, Social work in Communities and Organizations, Practicum Seminar, and Advanced Practice with Individuals and Families. Number of Hours Per Week Varies based on course schedule (maximum five course per academic year) Number of Months per Year 9 Hiring Range Three credit hour course: $3,588 per course for masters level and $3987 for a PhD Posting Details Posting Date 07/08/2026 Closing Date 09/01/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire 01/11/2027 Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/01/2026 Search Chair Name Mark Trahan Search Chair Email trahanmh@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board: 1. Letter of Interest/Cover Letter that includes interest in teaching and teaching-related experience. 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. List of References with Contact Information 4. A copy of unofficial graduate degree transcripts Official transcripts will be requested later. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
