    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55857": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Food Services Supervisor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Food Services Supervisor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please list a minimum of 3 professional references in the application. Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Position Summary Information Classification Title Food Services Supervisor-ASU Working Title Food Services Supervisor Location Boone, NC Job Category 8 Position Number 038391 Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Department Campus Dining - Park Place Cafe - 170450 Primary Purpose of Position To be an effective supervisor for Appalachian State University Campus Dining in both All Access units. The primary duties of the person in this role are to manage staff and supervise daily front-of-house operations in a university dining hall. This includes ensuring compliance with relevant codes and regulations. This is an evening position, responsible for the closing of the unit. This role must stay until closing each night to ensure that the unit is shut down properly.Appalachian Campus Dining exists to provide students, staff, faculty, and guests of the university nutritious, high quality meals, excellent services, and reasonable prices in a timely and efficient manner. Minimum Qualifications Graduation from High School or possession of a GED , and one year of experience in food preparation or service activities in a commercial kitchen; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Experience in the field of work related to the position’s role may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Special Note: This is a generalized representation of positions in this class and is not intended to reflect essential functions per ADA . Examples of competencies are typical of the majority of positions, but not be applicable to all positions. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Areas and duties under this employee’s purview include, but are not limited to the following: Front-line service , which means serving food to our guests and providing our student body with an excellent all-access dining experience by providing “unreasonable hospitality.” Housekeeping activities for an entire dining hall service area, including maintaining a clean serving area and dining room Supervise Food Service Technicians in preparing fresh fruits and vegetables for service on the salad bar, as well as making sure that all dry and pre-made foods are stocked, including desserts, snacks, breakfast foods, etc. Managing service lines to ensure that our customers fast, friendly and efficient customer service. Managing staff , including time and attendance, breaks any staff disciplinary issues that may arise. Duties also include ensuring uniform compliance and making sure that staff are ready and fit for duty every day. Staffing includes a mixture of full-time employees and part-time student employees. Working with and managing students is an important part of the function of this position. The Front-of-House supervisor will communicate with kitchen personnel, including chefs, sous chefs, and cooks, to ensure timely production and distribution of food. Managing inventory of food and supplies and placing orders when necessary. This includes management of perishable goods inventory, using first-in/first-out practices, and managing dated products, including “use by”, “best by” and “made on” dates. Managing the proper shutdown of the unit every night. This includes proper cleaning, food storage, equipment breakdown, sanitation and prep for the next day. A nightly walk through will be completed to ensure that the unit is properly closed and ready to open for the next day. Managing and maintaining the serving area , including stocking serving wares and other accoutrements, and stocking and maintaining drink lines. Managing our order-ahead queue. Maintaining proper sanitation standards throughout the servery, dining room, and restrooms. Supervisors need to adhere to proper food handling procedures, as delineated by North Carolina food code. Supervisors will earn and maintain their ServeSafe food manager certification and be responsible for ensuring that food handling practices are compliant with NC food code. Being available as an allergy resource and answering questions regarding allergen information for menu items and other dietary restrictions. Supervisors will also take allergy training and be able to answer student questions concerning allergen information and dietary restrictions. This role is that of a floor supervisor, and as such, the supervisor needs to be on the floor and visible at all times. The supervisor should be available to answer questions about dietary needs, handle customer concerns and complaints, and direct staff. This role will supervise and manage all aspects of daily customer service, and as such will have to manage multiple facets of the operation at once. This is a working supervisor position in a fast-paced environment. This role will require flexibility , including possible schedule changes and even being asked to cover other venues on campus. This is a mandatory position, meaning that the person in this role is required to be here in inclement weather or disasters, even in cases when the university must shut down. This role is mostly a working supervisor position , but does include a small administrative component, including placing orders when needed, maintaining temperature logs, tracking time and attendance, entering work orders and maintenance requests, technology troubleshooting, running a register when needed, and filing reports, including end-of-shift reports, etc. Any and all additional duties as directed or assigned by our supervisor. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Required for this Position Food service experience required Supervision experience Ability to direct large groups of employees Customer service skills Critical thinking, and problem-solving Knowledge of personnel management and food production Good time management and food safety skills Ability to delegate tasks to student and full-time employees In depth knowledge of the top 9 food allergens and how to prevent cross contact Preferred Qualifications Supervisory experience Experience in large-scale commercial dining Required Functional Competencies to Successfully Perform Job Duties. Knowledge-Technical: Understands preparation of large quantities of food, sanitation, weights, measures, and service techniques. Follows directives on order sheets. Supervises and evaluates the work of an entire full-time and student staff. Secures the unit. Operates equipment according to guidelines. Checks serving lines for eye appeal, adjusts as necessary. Orders food and / or supplies and completes work orders to equipment repairs. Notifies manager of any equipment needs. Training, follow-up, and coaching of all technical aspects of the kitchen, service, or dining area. Follows health laws in the preparation, holding, and storing of food. Provides records maintenance by completing allocation, accident, and exception reports. Planning and Organizing Work: Takes action to achieve goals beyond what is required by looking ahead and planning accordingly to the needs of the business and the customers both independently and with supervision. Plans work operations, establishes priorities, and sets deadlines over a short range period, within established goal and objectives. Arranges and assigns work. Customer Service: Greets customers pleasantly with a smile and good eye contact and enthusiastically. Customer service is enhanced by not reading, excessive talking, eating, drinking, or using tobacco products while in the Food Service unit. Handles customer complaints tactfully and pleasantly. Attentive to needs and comments from customers. Provides customers with correct information and or guidance as needed. Knows the mission of the organization and the value and role of customers in the work environment. Presents a positive image for Food Services. Recognizes potential problems in service, addresses, and resolves promptly and respectfully. Type of Position Permanent Full-Time Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours The hours for this position are 2:30 PM to 11:30 PM during the school year. Days of the week may vary. Summer hours also vary. Primary summer schedule hours for this shift are 11:30 AM to 8:30 PM. Employee may be required to work at least three home football games and/or any other special campus event. Schedules will be adjusted as needed to provide coverage for these events. Number of Hours Per Week 40 Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position Need to be able to lift at least 40 pounds. Be able to be on your feet 99% of the day. Be able to move constantly. Overall Competency Level Journey Salary Grade Equivalency Salary Range $24,408-$55,406 Anticipated Hiring Range $42,177 - $45,000 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date 09/20/2026 Competency Level Statement Management will only consider applicants who meet the required competencies. Special Instructions to Applicants Please list a minimum of 3 professional references in the application. Search Chair Name Travis Pierce Search Chair Email piercetk@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Departmental Information Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55856 Posting Number 201503039P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/46956": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Part Time Special Faculty of Health Care Management Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Part Time Special Faculty of Health Care Management Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter, including information about areas of expertise and interest in teaching online and/or face to face ● CV or Resume ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. Posting Details Request to Recruit Job Title Part Time Special Faculty of Health Care Management Department Nutrition & Health Care Mgt. - 273400 Location Boone, NC Position Number 085835 Description of Department The Health Care Management program began in 1972 and has been continuously certified by AUPHA since 1984. With over 1,400 graduates the program has a strong network of professionals working in health systems, physician practices, senior care organizations, and other health care organizations throughout North Carolina and the nation. Appalachian State University also offers an online Master of Health Administration degree that began in the fall of 2016 and is offering a new online Health Care Management program for adult learners in fall 2024. The Health Care Management program is located within the Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ). Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Health Administration, MBA , or related degree Essential Job Functions Primary instructional duties may include an introduction to healthcare systems, healthcare finance, healthcare law and ethics, human resources, leadership, and quality management in an online or face-to-face format at the undergraduate or graduate levels. Successful applicants will have a focus on teaching excellence in both the traditional face-to-face and online environments. Instructional duties may include a teaching load of up to six credit hours of online courses per semester. Undergraduate online courses follow shortened 8-week terms, and instructors are required to engage with students online on a regular basis, as defined by course material. Position may also require teaching in online format. Preferred Qualifications The department is especially interested in candidates with teaching interests in one or more of the following areas – introduction to healthcare systems, healthcare finance, healthcare law and ethics, human resources, leadership, and quality management in online or face to face format at the undergraduate or graduate level. Number of Hours Per Week Various, based on course schedule Number of Months per Year 12 Hiring Range Commensurate with experience Posting Details Posting Date 07/08/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled: Yes Proposed Date of Hire Evaluation of Applications Begins 07/08/2024 Search Chair Name Trent Spaulding Search Chair Email spauldingtj@appstate.edu Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter, including information about areas of expertise and interest in teaching online and/or face to face ● CV or Resume ● List of at least three references with contact information. Evaluations of applications are on a rolling basis as needed. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Comments Guest User Academic Affairs Comments Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55702": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Part-Time Administrative Assistant – External Engagement",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Part-Time Administrative Assistant – External Engagement Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Part-Time Administrative Assistant – External Engagement Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit resume, cover letter and a list of 3 professional references with contact inforamtion included Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Part-Time Administrative Assistant – External Engagement Location Boone, NC Position Number N01904 Department Management - 255300 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required 5+ years of relevant professional experience Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and entrepreneurial spirit, with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively Excellent written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated proficiency with common workplace tools (e.g., Microsoft Office, Google Workspace) and comfort working with design/communication platforms (e.g., Canva) Ability to work independently while also collaborating effectively with faculty, staff, and external partners Professional, approachable demeanor when interacting with a wide range of stakeholders License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Partner Identification & Outreach Support Assist in identifying and researching potential strategic partner organizations aligned with departmental priorities and program areas Maintain and update a centralized database of partners, prospects, and engagement activity Support initial outreach efforts and help track follow-up communication Communication & Relationship Support Coordinate and distribute monthly communications to partners, advisory council, alumni, and stakeholders Help maintain consistent, professional communication that strengthens relationships over time Support storytelling efforts by gathering updates on student experiences, internships, and partnerships Support the development and maintenance of the department’s external communications and digital presence, including social media and online platforms, to effectively share updates, highlight partnerships, and strengthen engagement with external stakeholders Program & Partner Coordination Help connect Program Directors and Coordinators with partner needs (e.g., internships, projects, mentorship opportunities) Assist in tracking partner engagement across programs to ensure alignment and visibility Support basic reporting on engagement activity and outcomes Event Coordination & Support Provide logistical and coordination support for key events such as NEXT in Management, The Night Before NEXT , Beyond NEXT , App on Tap, Advisory Council meetings, and other partner-facing initiatives Support the planning and execution of Advisory Council meetings, including scheduling, agenda development, materials preparation, communication, and follow-up Assist with scheduling, communication, materials preparation, and on-site coordination as needed across all events and engagements Help ensure a high-quality, professional experience for external partners, Advisory Council members, and participants Preferred Qualifications Interest in higher education, business, or relationship-building work preferred. Work Schedule/Hours Flexible work schedule, though attendance at events and meetings (both in-person and virtual) will be required. The position is for 20 hours each week for a 10-12 month period. Number of Hours Per Week 20 Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range $25.00 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 08/18/2026 Closing Date 10/02/2026 Open Until Filled No Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Submit resume, cover letter and a list of 3 professional references with contact inforamtion included Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55683 Posting Number 201500741P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
