    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/49695": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | PRN Physician Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources PRN Physician Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title PRN Physician Location Boone, North Carolina Position Number N32400 Department Health Services - 320000 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Minimal Qualifications required: Active medical practice (BE/BC) in Family Practice, Pediatrics, Internal Medicine, or Emergency Medicine and eligible for licensure in North Carolina. License/Certification Required Active medical practice (BE/BC) in family practice, pediatrics, internal medicine, or emergency medicine and eligible for licensure in North Carolina as a MD or DO A valid DEA license, NPI registration, updated basic CPR , eligibility for medical malpractice coverage, and other documentation for the health service’s credentialing process. A satisfactory criminal background report is required. Documentation of identity and employability of the applicant will be required before the hiring process can be finalized. Essential Job Functions The student health physician at the M.S. Shook Health Service is a Medical Doctor or Doctor of Osteopathy who is licensed to practice in North Carolina and is board eligible/board certified in Family Practice, Pediatrics, Internal Medicine, or Emergency Medicine. The student health physician reports to the Director of the Health Service. Specific duties of the student health physician include: • Provide out-patient ambulatory care for students with specific disease entities, injuries, minor surgical needs, and mental health problems; • Perform physical examinations, such as pre-participation sports physicals and gynecological exams; • Provide on-call services during evening and weekend hours during the regular academic school year; • Work cooperatively with Nurse Practitioners and/or Physician Assistants acting as a supervisor/consultant; • Refer patients requiring specialized care to competent consultants; • Collaborate with the Counseling Center in providing medical treatment for their clients; • Maintain confidential medical records which are completed in a timely manner; • Attend and participate in administrative conferences, in-service, and continuing education programs; • Act as a consultant and resource person for student and community health promotions, research projects, and health-related courses; • Serve on Health Service and university committees, as appropriate; • Adhere to regulatory guidelines and laws in the provision of care; • Keep credentials file current and complete, complying with required criteria and annual updates; • Accept other assignments as delegated by the Director of the Mary S. Shook Student Health Service. Preferred Qualifications Experience in college health or outpatient patient medicine. Work Schedule/Hours M-F 8-5, occasional weekends, as assigned on-call duties Number of Hours Per Week as needed Number of Months Per Year 11 Mandatory Staff Yes Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Hiring Range 91.16 Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 10/06/2021 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/30201 Posting Number 201500638P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55728": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Olympic Performance Dietitian Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Olympic Performance Dietitian Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Work experience or education that is NOT included on the application will NOT be considered when screening your application. Please include ALL work experience and education on the application to ensure that you receive the appropriate credit toward qualification for this position. Request to Recruit Working Title Olympic Performance Dietitian Location Boone, NC Position Number N38080 Department Athletics Office - 120000 Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Experience in nutrition for athletes. License/Certification Required Essential Job Functions Works under supervision of the Senior Associate Athletics Director for Student-Athlete Health and Well-Being. Assumes responsibility for the leadership, management, development, and oversight of the Department of Performance Nutrition for Olympic Sports. Oversees purchasing and budgeting of supplies and equipment for the Department of Performance Nutrition for Olympic Sports. Oversees inventory of supplies and equipment for the Department of Performance Nutrition for Olympic Sports. Oversees maintenance of all equipment for the Department of Performance Nutrition for Olympic Sports. Oversees and administers the development of a comprehensive nutrition program for Olympic Sports that focuses on injury prevention, athletic performance enhancement, and mental discipline in conjunction with members of the High Performance Team. Communicate and collaborate with student-athletes, administration, coaches, sports medicine, and other support staff on a daily basis. Oversees the development, review, and implementation of departmental policies and procedures. Oversees the operation of the App Fuel Station’s facilities. Organizes and administers weekly/monthly Department of Performance Nutrition staff meetings. Serve as a member of the department’s High Performance Team. Attends monthly High Performance Team meetings (when available). Directly oversees nutrition staff for Department of Performance Nutrition for Olympic Sports. Develop strategies to ensure that student-athletes are instructed and utilize proper nutritional habits. Facilitate integration of new sport specific nutritional strategies. Develop strategies to maximize athletic performance while minimizing occurrence of injury in a safe, structured training environment. Work in conjunction with the coaches to implement an inclusive nutritional program and implement year round programs. Maintain a positive visibility. Oversees the coordination of schedules and needs for App Fuel Stations. Maintain continuing education according to the requirements. (Certification) Abide by the rules as set forth by the National Collegiate Athletic Association, Southern Conference, and Sunbelt Conference. Performs miscellaneous related duties. Performs other duties as assigned by the Senior Associate Athletics Director for Student-Athlete Health and Well-Being. Preferred Qualifications Registered Dietitian ( RDN ), preferred Master’s, and at least one year of experience working in a collegiate or comparable setting as a student, GA, intern, fellow, or staff role.Experience Work Schedule/Hours 29 hours per week Number of Hours Per Week 29 hours per week Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Physical Demands of Position Must be able to lift at least 20 lbs., with or without reasonable accommodation. Hiring Range $20.00 to $30.00 per hour based on qualifications and experience Pay will be commensurate with applicant competencies, budget, equity and market considerations. Posting Details Information Posting Date 07/16/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Pool Preference External (Post on the Web) Special Instructions to Applicants Not Eligible for Visa Sponsorship Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55220 Posting Number 201501129P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54431": {
      "title": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant General Counsel",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant General Counsel Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant General Counsel Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the required documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume List of 3 Professional References with contact information included Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant General Counsel Location Boone, NC Faculty Rank No Provide Rank Position Number 093531 Department Office of General Counsel - 605000 Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Assistant General Counsel position will work in the Office of General Counsel to provide legal advice and counsel to the leaders of Appalachian State University. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must be admitted to the North Carolina bar or be admitted to the bar of another state and prepared to seek immediate admission in North Carolina within one year of the date of employment. License/Certification Required North Carolina State Bar membership in good standing, or licensure in good standing in another state on the date of initial employment and licensure to practice law in North Carolina within one year following initial employment date pursuant to The University of North Carolina Policy Manual, section 200.5. Preferred Qualifications Focused experience in one or more of the following areas is also preferred: IT/ ITS -related services; Contract review and drafting (particularly for higher education or governmental clients); Research, Intellectual Property, Sponsored Programs, and Regulatory Compliance Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Assistant General Counsel must demonstrate: high ethical standards, including a strong work ethic, honesty, and integrity; ability to identify and resolve legal issues; commitment to the support and fulfillment of the university’s mission; ability to employ excellent listening, oral, and written communication skills; interpersonal skills; research and analytical skills; reasoned judgment; ability to prioritize tasks and organize work; ability to supervise staff in the fulfillment of the office mission; ability to combine legal considerations with program and policy objectives in the development of practical solutions that meet client needs; word processing and related skills to create, edit, and publish legal memoranda, briefs, contracts, and other work products Type of Position Full Time Position Staff/Non-Faculty Staff/Non-Faculty VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Appointment Type 1.0 Work Schedule/Hours Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00pm. (may vary according to office commitments) Number of Hours Per Week 40 (may vary according to office commitments) Number of Months Per Year 12 Mandatory Staff No Suggested Salary Range $95,000 - $107,120 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Posting Date 04/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 05/26/2026 Proposed Date of Hire 08/03/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the required documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume List of 3 Professional References with contact information included Search Chair Name Sarah Rupp Search Chair Email ruppse@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54014 Posting Number 201501766P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
